COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[278,"§Safa\n‘Safa’ is the name of a mountain which is about 100 meters from the Holy Kaaba. It is mentioned once in the Holy Quran:\nإِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِن شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ\nIndeed, as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.\n[Al-Baqara: 158]\nSafa and Marwa are the two mountains between which the Hajis perform the ‘Sa’ee’ seven times remembering how Hajira ran between these two mountains in search of water (described in detail under the head ‘Marwa’). The Safa mountain is also connected with the life of the Holy Prophet(saws). In the Holy Quran, it is said to the Holy Prophet(saws):\n﴿وَأَنذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ الْأَقْرَبِينَ ٢١٤﴾\nAnd warn, [O Muhammad], your closest kindred.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 214]\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) climbed up the mountain Safa and called out loudly, “Ya Sabahah! If I told you that there were enemies on the other side of this mountain about to attack you, would you believe me!”\n“Yes. Why not? We have never known you to speak a lie.” Then the Messenger of Allah(swt) said, “I warn you of a terrible punishment.” The people were silent except for Abu Lahab who said, “May you perish for this! Did you only summon us for this!” After this incident, Surah-111, Surah-Al-Lahab was revealed:\n﴿تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِي لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ ١ مَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُ مَالُهُ وَمَا كَسَبَ ٢ سَيَصْلَىٰ نَارًا ذَاتَ لَهَبٍ ٣ وَامْرَأَتُهُ حَمَّالَةَ الْحَطَبِ ٤ فِي جِيدِهَا حَبْلٌ مِّن مَّسَدٍ ٥﴾\nMay the hands of Abu Lahab be ruined, and ruined is he.His wealth will not avail him or that which he gained.He will [enter to] burn in a Fire of [blazing] flame .And his wife [as well] - the carrier of firewood. Around her neck is a rope of [twisted] fiber.\n[Abu-Lahab: 1-5]\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 4770 and Sahih Muslim, 208)\nThis is the same Safa mountain from which the Holy Prophet(saws) made this declaration after the victory over Makkah:\n\"He who enters the house of Abu Sufyan will be safe, He who lays down arms will be safe, He who locks his door will be safe\"\n(See: Sahih Muslim, 1780, Conquest of Makkah)"],[279,"§Sahaba\n‘Sahaba’ are the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) who believed in his prophethood and in spite of all sorts of difficulties, never left his side. They have a very important place in Islam as it was through them that Islam reached us. Therefore they are described in various contexts in the Holy Quran. At one place it is said that Muhammad(saws) is the Messenger of Allah(swt) and the people with him are tough with the disbelievers but kind towards each other. [Al-Fath: 29]. That is, they were firm believers of Islam. At another place they are described as follows:\nكُنتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ تَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَتَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ وَتُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ ۗ\nYou are the best nation produced [as an example] for mankind. You enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong and believe in Allah.\n[Al-i-Imran: 110]\nAll the Muslims are addressed in the above verse but first and foremost the people meant are the sahaba.\nAt another place, Allah(swt) addresses only the sahaba as:\n﴿لَّقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّـهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ فَعَلِمَ مَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ فَأَنزَلَ السَّكِينَةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَأَثَابَهُمْ فَتْحًا قَرِيبًا ١٨﴾\nCertainly was Allah pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you, [O Muhammad], under the tree, and He knew what was in their hearts, so He sent down tranquillity upon them and rewarded them with an imminent conquest.\n[Al-Fath: 18]\nAllah(swt) clearly says in the Holy Quran that he is pleased with the Sahaba. When we study the lives of these sahaba, we come to know that after embracing Islam they had to face countless difficulties but they never left the side of the Holy Prophet(saws). They were thrown out of their homes, dragged through the scorching hot sand of the desert. When even then they did not leave Islam, they were whipped and were forced to leave their homeland and migrate (See: ‘Hijrat’). This was because they believed in Allah(swt) and this did not please the idolators of Makkah who tortured them in every possible manner. In the face of all these, these sahaba were courageous and patient and this pleased Allah(swt) and He(swt) made their lives an example of true belief till the Last Day and forever. That is why it is not proper to say anything bad about these sahaba. In this regard the Holy Prophet(saws) has said:\n\"Do not say anything bad about my Companions. If any of you were to spend the weight of Uhud in gold, it still would not reach the measure (mudd) of one of them nor even one-half of it.\"\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 3673 and Sahih Muslim, 2540)\nThe number of Sahabas:\nWe do not have the list of the names of the people who embraced Islam during the life of the Holy Prophet(saws), but at the time of the death of the Holy Prophet(saws) their number was more than one lakh twenty thousand because one lakh Sahabas performed the Hajj along with the Holy Prophet(saws) and many were in Madina and other places and could not take part in the Hajj.\nThe first Sahaba to embrace Islam:\n1.The first among children to embrace Islam was Ali-bin-Abu-Talib, son of the paternal uncle of the Holy Prophet(saws) and also his son-in-law.\n2.The first woman to embrace Islam was Khadija-bint-Khuwailid(ra), the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws).\n3.The first man to embrace Islam was Abu-Bakr Siddique(ra), the first Khalifa of the Muslims and the father-in-law and friend of the Holy Prophet(saws).\n4.The first freed slave to embrace Islam was Zaid-bin-Haris who was presented to the Holy Prophet(saws) by Khadija to serve him. The Holy Prophet(saws) then freed him, but Zaid-bin-Haris chose to remain with him.\nThe prominent Sahabas:\nAmong the prominent Sahabas, the foremost are the four Khalifas – Khulfa-e-Rashideen (the rightly guided). They were:\n1.Abu-Bakr Siddique(ra):\nThe Muslims are unanimous in their opinion that after the Holy Prophet(saws), Abu-Bakr was the best. That is why on the very day of the death of the Holy Prophet(saws), the people of Madina took pledge on his hand as the successor of the Holy Prophet(saws). In case somebody could not do so on the first day, they took pledge later on.\nThe period of his leadership was two years, three months and eight days. He died in 13 A.H. He was sixty-three. He is considered the best among the Sahabas. He accompanied the Holy Prophet(saws) during his migration from Makkah to Madina. Abu-Bakr was convinced that the disbelievers of Makkah would follow them, so instead of taking the northern route which led directly to Madina, he took the southern route and both of them hid in a cave for three days. When the enemies reached the mouth of the cave, Abu-Bakr feared that if they looked down, they would be seen and captured. But the Holy Prophet(saws) was calm and composed and reassured Abu-Bakr not to panic as Allah(swt) was with them. The Holy Quran says about this incident:\n﴿إِلَّا تَنصُرُوهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللَّـهُ إِذْ أَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ثَانِيَ اثْنَيْنِ إِذْ هُمَا فِي الْغَارِ إِذْ يَقُولُ لِصَاحِبِهِ لَا تَحْزَنْ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ مَعَنَا ۖ فَأَنزَلَ اللَّـهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَيْهِ وَأَيَّدَهُ بِجُنُودٍ لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلَىٰ ۗ وَكَلِمَةُ اللَّـهِ هِيَ الْعُلْيَا ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ ٤٠﴾\nIf you do not aid the Prophet - Allah has already aided him when those who disbelieved had driven him out [of Makkah] as one of two, when they were in the cave and he said to his companion, \"Do not grieve; indeed Allah is with us.\" And Allah sent down his tranquillity upon him and supported him with angels you did not see and made the word of those who disbelieved the lowest, while the word of Allah - that is the highest. And Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\n[At-Tawba: 40]\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was convinced that as Allah(swt) had sent him as the Last Prophet, He(swt) would help him. Surah-Ma’ida was revealed in Madina, but its verse\nوَاللَّهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ\nAnd Allah will protect you from the people.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 67]\nIs a miracle which proved true both before and after the migration.\nThe excellence of Abu-Bakr is narrated in many sahih hadith. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“I declare my innocence before Allah(swt) that I should have any bosom friend among you for Allah Most High has taken me as His friend just as He took Ibrahim as His friend. If I were to take any bosom friend from my nation I would take Abu Bakr.”\n(Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, 2383)\n2.Umar-bin-Khattab(ra):\nHe was made a Khalifa in 13 A.H. and was martyred in 23 A.H. The one who martyred him was a Parsi slave named Abu-Lulu Firoz. His Khilafat lasted for ten years and six and a half months. He was the first Khalifa to be called ‘Ameerul-Momineen’. He was sixty-three when he was martyred. The most important battles which took place during his time were the battles of Yarmouk, Qadisiya and Nahavand in which the Muslim armies were successful and the Islamic reign spread from the Arabian peninsula to Syria, Iran and Iraq. His excellence has been narrated in various sahih hadith. He was such a staunch Muslim that on one occasion the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n\"By Him in Whose Hands my life is, whenever Satan sees you taking a path, he follows a path other than yours.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3294 and Sahih Muslim, 2396)\n“There were some people from the Bani-Israel who were not prophets but had divine inspirations.If it had been someone from my ummah, it would be Umar.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3689 and Sahih Muslim, 2398)\nThat is, the thoughts and actions of Umar-bin-Khattab were as if he had had some divine inspiration from Allah(swt). It is narrated by Umar(ra) himself that Allah(swt) had agreed with him in three things – Maqaam-e-Ibraheem, Purdah and the prisoners of Badr. That is, in these three cases verses of the Holy Quran were revealed according to the wishes of Umar. (See Sahih Muslim, 2399)\n3.Usman-bin-Affan(ra):\nHe was the third Khalifa of the Muslims. Umar-bin-Khattab had formed a committee of six prominent Sahabas to choose a Khalifa after him. They were:\n1.Usman-bin-Affan(ra).\n2.Ali-bin-Abu Talib(ra).\n3.Talha-bin-Ubaydullah(ra).\n4.Sad-bin-Abi Waqqas(ra).\n5.Abdur-Rehman-bin-Ouf(ra).\n6.Zubair-bin-Awwam(ra).\nHe then said, “You elect a Khalifa from among yourselves.” Everyone chose Usman-bin-Affan(ra) as the next Khalifa.\nIn this way, after the martyrdom of Umar(ra), Usman(ra) became the Khalifa in 24 A.H. and was martyred in 35 A.H. His reign was for ten days less than twelve years. Among his killers were Kinana-in-Bishr, Khutaira Sakoni and Abdur-Rehman-bin-Udays who were all Egyptians. During his reign, the Islamic kingdom had spread till Northern Africa.\nHis excellence has been narrated in many sahih hadith. It can be gauged from the fact that after the death of his daughter, the Holy Prophet(saws) got his other daughter also married to Usman(ra). It was well-known that Usman(ra) was very bashful. It is narrated that one day the Holy Prophet(saws) was lying down in the house of Aisha(ra) and a part of his calf was exposed. Abu-Bakr(ra) knocked at the door and sought permission to enter. He got the permission and entered. After some time Umar(ra) entered in the same way and the Holy Prophet(saws) kept lying down in the same way. After some time Usman(ra) knocked and sought permission to enter. The Holy Prophet(saws) got up and adjusted his garment.\nAisha(ra) asked the Holy Prophet(saws) later:\n“When Abu-Bakr came, you kept lying down as you were, when Umar came, you remained in the same position. But when Usman came, you sat up properly and straightened your clothes.” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “How can I not feel bashful in front of the person before whom even the angels feel bashful.”\n(See: Sahih Muslim, 2401)\n4.Ali-bin-Abu-Talib(ra):\nHe was the son of the paternal uncle of the Holy Prophet(saws), Abu-Talib and the husband of his favourite daughter Fatima(ra). The very day Usman(ra) was martyred, the people of Madina took the pledge of Ali(ra) being the next Khalifa in 35 A.H. Then he went away from Madina to Kufa where he was martyred in 40 A.H. by Abdur-Rehman-bin-Muljim. He was sixty-three at the time. Thus his reign was for four years, nine months and ten days. His excellence is narrated in many sahih hadith. One is the following incident:\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) was setting out for the battle of Tabuk, he(saws) asked Ali(ra) to stay back and take care of the womenfolk and the children. Ali(ra) said, “O Apostle of Allah(swt)! You are leaving me behind with the women and children? (that is, you are not taking me with you on jihad).” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “O Ali! Aren’t you pleased with the fact that you are to me like Haroon was to Musa. But no prophet will come after me.” (See: Sahih Bukhari, 4416 and Sahih Muslim, 2404)\nThe number of the Sahabas narrating the hadith:\nAs mentioned earlier, the number of Sahabas at the time of the death of the Holy Prophet(saws) was about one lakh twenty thousand. The life histories of more than thirteen thousand sahabas can be found in various books today and out of them more than a thousand are the ones who have narrated the hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws). Bakhi-bin-Makhlad who was a great scholar of hadith died in 276 A.H. In his ‘Musnad’ the hadith narrated by more than a thousand sahabas can be found. From among them, ten sahabas have been described here:\n1.Abu-Huraira(ra): He has narrated the greatest number of hadith, that is 5374. After embracing Islam, he came from Yemen to Madina and started serving the Holy Prophet(saws). His custom was to be seated near the door of the Holy Prophet(saws) and whenever he(saws) went out, he would accompany him. Whatever the Holy Prophet(saws) said, he remembered. He once complained to the Holy Prophet(saws) about his memory being weak and the Holy Prophet(saws) prayed for him. Abu-Huraira said that after that he never forgot anything.\n2.Abdullah-bin-Umar-bin-Khattab(ra): The hadith narrated by him were 2630.\n3.Anas-bin-Malik(ra): The hadith narrated by him were 2236.\n4.Aisha-bint-Abu-Bakr(ra): She was the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws) and the hadith narrated by her were 2210.\n5.Abdullah-bin-Abbas(ra): He narrated 1660 hadith.\n6.Jabir-bin-Abdullah(ra): He narrated 1540 hadith.\n7.Abu-Saeed-Khudri(ra): He narrated 1170 hadith.\n8.Abdullah-bin-Masood(ra): He narrated 848 hadith.\n9.Abdullah-bin-Amr-bin-Aas(ra): He narrated 700 hadith.\n10.Umar-bin-Khattab(ra): He narrated 537 hadith.\nThe numbers mentioned above have been taken from ‘Jawamiah Seerat’ by Hafiz Ibn-Hazam, which is in turn based on ‘Musnad’ of Bakhi-bin-Makhlad. He has also said that if someone finds some more hadith, then he should add them to this number. So, it is possible that there is an increase in the above given numbers. (See p.315)\nAbout the exact number of hadith it can be said that we have about sixty to seventy thousand hadith spread out in hundreds of books. The number of chains of narrators of these hadith is about three lakhs. A German scholar who has edited a book titled Isaba and published it from Kolkata, writes in his foreword that the number of narrators is around five lakhs. Their life histories have been preserved in the books of Asma-Ur-Rijal. But all these sixty to seventy thousand hadith are not authentic. After a lot of research it has been concluded that the sahih or authentic hadith are about fifteen thousand which are spread out in hundreds of books. It is now most important to separate the authentic hadith from the ‘Zaeef’ ones because these cannot form the pillar of Islam.\nThe sahabas whose names occur in the Holy Quran:\nThe sahaba whose name occurs in the Holy Quran is Zaid(ra). He was from the Arab tribe. His full name was Zaid-bin-Haritha-bin-Sharaheel Al-Kambi, but somebody kidnapped him when he was a child and sold him as a slave. Khadija(ra), the first wife of the Holy Prophet(saws) bought him and presented him to the Holy Prophet(saws) to serve him. The Holy Prophet(saws) freed him and adopted him. Then he married him to Zainab-bint-Jahsh, the daughter of his paternal aunt, Umaimah-bint-Abdul-Mutallib. But both of them could not get along. There were many differences and hence divorce was being considered. Then, through a revelation it was prophesied that a divorce would take place and then Zainab would be married to the Holy Prophet(saws). In those days it was unlawful to marry the wife of one’s adopted son as it was unlawful to marry the wife of one’s own son. To end this practice it was necessary for Zainab to be married to the Holy Prophet(saws). The Holy Prophet(saws) knew everything but was hesitating in doing the right thing fearing what the people would say. He kept asking Zaid to fear Allah(swt) and not divorce Zainab. Then the following verses of Surah-33, Al-Ahzab were revealed:\n﴿وَإِذْ تَقُولُ لِلَّذِي أَنْعَمَ اللَّـهُ عَلَيْهِ وَأَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِ أَمْسِكْ عَلَيْكَ زَوْجَكَ وَاتَّقِ اللَّـهَ وَتُخْفِي فِي نَفْسِكَ مَا اللَّـهُ مُبْدِيهِ وَتَخْشَى النَّاسَ وَاللَّـهُ أَحَقُّ أَن تَخْشَاهُ ۖ فَلَمَّا قَضَىٰ زَيْدٌ مِّنْهَا وَطَرًا زَوَّجْنَاكَهَا لِكَيْ لَا يَكُونَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ حَرَجٌ فِي أَزْوَاجِ أَدْعِيَائِهِمْ إِذَا قَضَوْا مِنْهُنَّ وَطَرًا ۚ وَكَانَ أَمْرُ اللَّـهِ مَفْعُولًا ٣٧﴾\nAnd [remember, O Muhammad], when you said to the one on whom Allah bestowed favor and you bestowed favor, \"Keep your wife and fear Allah,\" while you concealed within yourself that which Allah is to disclose. And you feared the people, while Allah has more right that you fear Him. So when Zayd had no longer any need for her, We married her to you in order that there not be upon the believers any discomfort concerning the wives of their adopted sons when they no longer have need of them. And ever is the command of Allah accomplished.\n[Al-Ahzab: 37]\nZainab would proudly say that Allah(swt) himself married her to the Holy Prophet(saws).\nThe ten sahaba who were given glad tidings of paradise were:\n1.Abu-Bakr-Siddique-bin-Abu-Kuhafa(ra). Expired: 13 A.H.\n2.Umar-bin-Khattab(ra). Expired: 23 A.H.\n3.Usman-bin-Affan(ra). Expired: 35 A.H.\n4.Ali-bin-Abu-Talib(ra). Expired: 40 A.H.\n5.Zubair-bin-Awwam(ra). Expired: 36 A.H.\n6.Talha-bin-Ubaidullah(ra). Expired: 36 A.H.\n7.Abdur-Rehman-bin-Ouf(ra). Expired: 32 A.H.\n8.Abu-Ubaida-bin-Zarrah(ra). Expired: 18 A.H.\n9.Saeed-bin-Zaid-Adwi(ra). Expired: 50 A.H.\n10.Sad-bin-Abi-Waqqas(ra). Expired: 55 A.H.\nSad-bin-Abi-Waqqas(ra) was the last to die among the people who were to enter the paradise.\nThe above mentioned ten sahabas are the ones who were given the glad tidings of paradise by the Holy Prophet(saws) in one sahih hadith. Other than these many other sahabas were given the good news of paradise at other times.\nPopular Arabic books written about the lives of these sahabas:\nWhile hundreds of books have been written about the lives of the sahabas, a few are being mentioned here:\n1.Mojam Sahaba by Abdul-Baaki-bin-Kane’a (Expired: 351 A.H.)\n2.Maarifatus-Sahaba by Abu Nuaim Isfahani (Expired: 430 A.H.)\n3.Al-Istiaab by Yusuf-bin-Abdullah-bin-Ibn-Abdul-Barr (Expired: 463 A.H.)\n4.Usdul Ghaaba Fi Maarifatus-Sahaba by Izzuddin Abul-Hasan Muhammad-bin-Muhammad-ibn-Aseer (Expired: 620 A.H.)\n5.Tajreed Asma-e-Sahaba by Shamsuddin Zahabi (Expired: 748 A.H.)\n6. Al-Isaba Fi Tameezis-Sahaba by Ahmad-bin-Ali-Ibn-Hajar (Expired: 852 A.H.)\nToday, Islam is the only religion in which the life histories of the Holy Prophet(saws), his companions, their disciples, and the disciples of those disciples; that is the complete life histories of all those people till the fifth century have been preserved. These people are called ‘Raavi’ or ‘narrators’ of hadith. This is to facilitate the research of the various hadith to determine whether they are authentic (sahih) or innovated or ‘Zaeef’. This depends on the narrator of the hadith. If the narrator is ‘truthful’ or ‘siqah’ in the hadith terminology, then the hadith narrated by him will be ‘sahih’ or ‘authentic’ or ‘truthful’ or ‘reliable’. And if the narrator is not truthful, then the hadith narrated by him will be ‘Zaeef’ or ‘not reliable’. But other than the character of the narrators, there are many other things to be considered before labeling a hadith as ‘sahih’ or ‘Zaeef’ and it is beyond the scope of this book to go into them. But it is very important for the narrator to be truthful in calling his hadith ‘sahih’. Among the many things to be considered about a narrator, two points are very important:\n1.Firstly, by his actions and behavior a narrator should be a true Muslim of excellent character who fulfills the obligatory acts and avoids the unlawful acts; that is, he leads his life according to the teachings of Islam.\n2.Secondly, his memory must be sound. He must be able to remember and repeat exactly what he has heard from his teacher. If he writes it down, it is even better.\nIf both the above qualities are found in a ‘Raavi’ or ‘narrator’, then he is called a ‘Siqah Raavi’ which means ‘a truthful narrator’ and the hadith narrated by him will be considered ‘sahih’. If both the above qualities or even one of them is not found in any narrator, then the narrator will be called ‘Zaeef’ and the hadith narrated by him will be termed ‘Zaeef’. This principle is used in researching the hadith and is specific to Islam and Muslims. It cannot be employed in any other religion."],[280,"§Saheefa\n‘Saheefa’ means a religious book, whose plural form is ‘Suhuf’. This plural form has been used at various places in the Holy Quran which are as follows:\n1.Saheefas of Ibraheem(as):\nThe saheefas of Ibraheem(as) are described at two places in the Holy Quran.\nOne in Surah-An-Najm:\n﴿أَمْ لَمْ يُنَبَّأْ بِمَا فِي صُحُفِ مُوسَىٰ ٣٦ وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ الَّذِي وَفَّىٰ ٣٧ أَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ ٣٨ وَأَن لَّيْسَ لِلْإِنسَانِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ ٣٩ وَأَنَّ سَعْيَهُ سَوْفَ يُرَىٰ ٤٠ ثُمَّ يُجْزَاهُ الْجَزَاءَ الْأَوْفَىٰ ٤١﴾\nOr has he not been informed of what was in the scriptures of Moses. And [of] Abraham, who fulfilled [his obligations] - That no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another. And that there is not for man except that [good] for which he strives. And that his effort is going to be seen - Then he will be recompensed for it with the fullest recompense.\n[An-Najm: 36-41]\nWhen we read the verses of Surah-An-Najm from verse-36 to the end of the surah, we understand that everything was present in the sahifas of Ibraheem(as). We no longer have them on earth, but the teachings described in the Holy Quran are in fact the very truths preached by all the other prophets. But, some people have distorted them and made Isa(as) their ‘Saviour’. (See Bible, Luke 2:11)\nSecond, in Surah-Al-A’la, in which it says:\n﴿هَـٰذَا لَفِي الصُّحُفِ الْأُولَىٰ ١٨ صُحُفِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَمُوسَىٰ ١٩﴾\nIndeed, this is in the former scriptures, The scriptures of Abraham and Moses.\n[Al-A’la: 18, 19]\nThat is, all the nineteen verses of Surah-Al-A’la were present in the Saheefas of Ibraheem(as) and also in the Saheefas of Musa(as). This is narrated by Ibn-Abbas also. (See: Tafseer Ibn-Abi Haatim 1:3419)\n2.Saheefas of Musa(as):\nThe description of the Saheefas of Musa(as) has already been done in the Saheefas of Ibraheem(as).\nGenesis, Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers and Deuteronomy are the first five books of Bible. They are called the ‘Taurah’. They were revealed to Musa(as). But many things were distorted in it. There are still many things in it which are corroborated by the Holy Quran. These are the things which are described as guidance and light.\n(See : Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-44-46)\nIn the same way, some parts of the Saheefas of Musa(as) have been described in the Holy Quran. (See: Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verses-32, 45 and Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-145)\nIn fact at one place, expressing surprise, the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَكَيْفَ يُحَكِّمُونَكَ وَعِندَهُمُ التَّوْرَاةُ فِيهَا حُكْمُ اللَّـهِ ثُمَّ يَتَوَلَّوْنَ مِن بَعْدِ ذَٰلِكَ ۚ وَمَا أُولَـٰئِكَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ ٤٣﴾\nBut how is it that they come to you for judgement while they have the Torah, in which is the judgement of Allah? Then they turn away, [even] after that; but those are not [in fact] believers.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 43]\n3.The word ‘Suhuf’ has been used for the Holy Quran also. (See Quran, Surah-80, Abasa, Verses 13-15 and Surah-98, Al-Bayyina, Verse-2)\n4.The word ‘Suhuf’ has also been used for ‘book of deeds’. (See Quran, Surah-81, At-Takwir, Verse-10)\n5.The word ‘Suhuf’ has also been used for ‘scrolls of revelation’ (See: Quran, Surah-74, Al-Muddathir, Verse-52)"],[281,"§Sail Al-Arim\n‘Sail’ means ‘flood’ and ‘Arim’ means ‘dam’. Therefore ‘Sail Al-Arim’ means ‘flood released from the dam’. This is described only once in the Holy Quran:\nفَأَعْرَضُوا فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَيْلَ الْعَرِمِ\nBut they turned away [refusing], so We sent upon them the flood of the dam.\n[Saba: 16]\n‘Saba’ was a tribe of Yemen which was very prosperous. (See: ‘Saba’). One reason for their prosperity was trade. The second was the dam which they had built between the mountains to store water for irrigation. As a result their tribe was extremely prosperous even in agriculture. There was greenery everywhere. With so many favours from Allah(swt), the least they could do was to follow the path of Allah(swt), thank Him and obey His Commands. But instead, they became proud and arrogant. They transgressed the limits and disobeyed Allah(swt). So, they incurred the wrath of Allah(swt) and He(swt) sent the flood of the dam upon them. The cities which were inter-connected became desolate, all the crops were destroyed. The survivors fled Yemen. The Ghassanids fled to Syria and the Khajraj went to Madina, which was called ‘Yathrib’ in those days. Banu Khuza’a went to Jeddah and Makkah. Thus the tribe of ‘Saba’ no longer existed in Yemen. Only a few were left who believed in ‘monotheism’. The Holy Quran describes this as follows:\n﴿فَأَعْرَضُوا فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَيْلَ الْعَرِمِ وَبَدَّلْنَاهُم بِجَنَّتَيْهِمْ جَنَّتَيْنِ ذَوَاتَيْ أُكُلٍ خَمْطٍ وَأَثْلٍ وَشَيْءٍ مِّن سِدْرٍ قَلِيلٍ ١٦ ذَٰلِكَ جَزَيْنَاهُم بِمَا كَفَرُوا ۖ وَهَلْ نُجَازِي إِلَّا الْكَفُورَ ١٧ وَجَعَلْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ الْقُرَى الَّتِي بَارَكْنَا فِيهَا قُرًى ظَاهِرَةً وَقَدَّرْنَا فِيهَا السَّيْرَ ۖ سِيرُوا فِيهَا لَيَالِيَ وَأَيَّامًا آمِنِينَ ١٨ فَقَالُوا رَبَّنَا بَاعِدْ بَيْنَ أَسْفَارِنَا وَظَلَمُوا أَنفُسَهُمْ فَجَعَلْنَاهُمْ أَحَادِيثَ وَمَزَّقْنَاهُمْ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍ ۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُورٍ ١٩ وَلَقَدْ صَدَّقَ عَلَيْهِمْ إِبْلِيسُ ظَنَّهُ فَاتَّبَعُوهُ إِلَّا فَرِيقًا مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ٢٠﴾\nBut they turned away [refusing], so We sent upon them the flood of the dam, and We replaced their two [fields of] gardens with gardens of bitter fruit, tamarisks and something of sparse lote trees.[By] that We repaid them because they disbelieved. And do We [thus] repay except the ungrateful? And We placed between them and the cities which We had blessed [many] visible cities. And We determined between them the [distances of] journey, [saying], \"Travel between them by night or day in safety.\" But [insolently] they said, \"Our Lord, lengthen the distance between our journeys,\" and wronged themselves, so We made them narrations and dispersed them in total dispersion. Indeed in that are signs for everyone patient and grateful.And Iblees had already confirmed through them his assumption, so they followed him, except for a party of believers.\n[Saba: 16-20]\nThis dam of ‘Saba’ which is described in the historical records broke in 542 A.D. It was 1760 ft long and 60 ft wide. Many kings helped in building this dam. The valley in which this dam was built is called even today as ‘Arim’. It had broken once before in the 6th century; but it completely broke in 542 A.D. and the tribe of ‘Saba’ was permanently scattered. This is the rule of Allah(swt). He(swt) gives the disbelievers a free hand for sometime. Then one day he seizes them in such a way that they are totally wiped out and we can come to know about them only from history. A few remains of this dam can still be found. In 1843 A.D, a Frenchman named Arnold managed to go to the place where this dam existed. He says about this dam that it was built between two mountains with the help of mud and stones. These days, pathways have been built in the lower part of the mountains to let out water into the fields for irrigation. Huge and heavy gates have been built to shut these doors. Water is let out as needed and then the gates are shut.\nIt is said that during the reign of different kings, the height of the dam kept on being increased and it was finally completed in 300 A.D. Then it was totally destroyed in 542 A.D."],[282,"§Sajdah\n‘Sajdah’ means ‘prostration’, that is to rest the forehead on the ground. Before the advent of Islam, people prostrated before idols and kings. But Islam forbids the prostration before anyone other than Allah(swt) as it goes against the basic tenet of Islam namely ‘monotheism’ and this was what was preached by all the prophets. (See ‘Ruku’)\nThe correct way of performing the ‘sajdah’ is to rest the seven organs – forehead, two hands, two knees and two palms on the ground such that the stomach is raised from the ground and the palms are on either side of the head and then very calmly glorify Allah(swt). It is narrated in the sahih hadith that in the state of prostration, a slave is closest to Allah(swt).\n‘Sajdah’ is an essential pillar of Namaz, without which namaz is not complete. Therefore it is ‘shirk’ to prostrate before anyone other than Allah(swt). A person doing so is no more a Muslim.\nThe verses related to ‘sajdah’ have already been described under ‘Ruku’."],[283,"§Salam\nWhen we meet and greet each other, the word used is ‘Salam’. In Islam, the method and importance of Salam has been explained. Salam is a way of praying for each other and also conveying best wishes.\nWhen the dwellers of paradise meet each other, they will say ‘Salam’ to each other. (See: Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-10)\nThe gatekeepers of paradise will say ‘Salam’ to those who enter it.\n(See:Quran, Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-73)\nThe angels who take the souls of the good and pious people first greet them saying ‘Salam’.\n(See:Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-32)\n‘Salam’ has great importance in Islam. In fact it is obligatory for a Muslim to greet another Muslim with ‘Salam’ when he meets him. (Sahih Bukhari, 124 and Sahih Muslim, 2162)\nA man asked the Holy Prophet(saws) as to what the best action in Islam was.The Holy Prophet(saws) replied,\n“Feeding people and saying salam to the one you know and to the one you do not know.” (Sahih Bukhari, 12 and Sahih Muslim, 39)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“O People! Say salam to each other and feed each other. Pray when the others are asleep (that is, pray the Tahajjud namaz) and you will reach paradise in safety.”\n(Tirmizi: 2485)\nThe best person is the one who is the first to say ‘Salam’. (See Abu-Dawood 5197 and Tirmizi 2694)\nThe rider should first say salam to the pedestrian and the pedestrian should first say salam to the one who is sitting down and in the case of two pedestrians, the better one is the one who says salam first. (See: Ibn-Hibban 498)\nA man came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and said:\nA man came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and said: “Assalamu-alaikum!” The Holy Prophet(saws) greeted him back and he sat down. The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Ten.” That is, you get ten rewards. Then another man came and said to the Holy Prophet(saws) “Assalamu-alaikum wa Rahmatullah!” The Holy Prophet(saws) greeted him back and he also sat down. The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Twenty.” That is, you get twenty rewards.” A third man then came up and said, “Assalamu-alaikum wa Rahmatullahi wa Barakatuh!” The Holy Prophet(saws) greeted him back and said, “Thirty.” That is, you get thirty rewards. (Abu Dawood 5195 and Tirmizi 2689)"],[284,"§Sa-la-wat\nIn the Holy Quran, ‘Sa-la-wat’ has been used for the worship-houses of the Jews, the synagogues. It has been said in the Holy Quran that Allah(swt) checks some people with the help of others and were it not so, the monasteries, churches, synagogues etc. where the name of Allah(swt) was recited would have been razed and this earth would have been a place of chaos and confusion. The Holy Quran says:\nالَّذِينَ أُخْرِجُوا مِن دِيَارِهِم بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ إِلَّا أَن يَقُولُوا رَبُّنَا اللَّهُ ۗ وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ اللَّهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُم بِبَعْضٍ لَّهُدِّمَتْ صَوَامِعُ وَبِيَعٌ وَصَلَوَاتٌ وَمَسَاجِدُ يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا اسْمُ اللَّهِ كَثِيرًا ۗ\n[They are] those who have been evicted from their homes without right - only because they say, \"Our Lord is Allah.\" And were it not that Allah checks the people, some by means of others, there would have been demolished monasteries, churches, synagogues, and mosques in which the name of Allah is much mentioned.\n[Al-Hajj: 40]"],[285,"§Saleh(as)\nSaleh(as) was from the tribe of Nuh(as). His paternal grandfather was ‘Thamud’ and his tribe was later on known as the tribe of Thamud.\nSome scholars are of the opinion that he lived about three hundred years before Ibraheem(as). He lived in Hijr, which is between Hijaz and Tabook. The Holy Quran says about the people of Hijr:\nوَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ أَصْحَابُ الْحِجْرِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ\nAnd certainly did the companions of Thamud deny the messengers.\n[Al-Hijr: 80]\nThe tribe of Thamud is also described in the books of Arastu and Batlimos. And it is said that these people lived near Domatha which is called Dumat Al-Jandal today.\nIn the Bible ( Genesis 10:11), the family tree from Nuh(as) to Ibraheem(as) has been depicted as under:\nNuh(as)\nJapheth Ham Shem\nArphaxad\nSaleh\nEber\nPeleg\nReu\nSerug\nNahor\nTerah\nIbraheem(as)\nSome scholars are of the opinion that Peleg, the son of Eber is called Saleh because the Samud lived about three hundred years before Ibraheem(as). Some scholars say Saleh, the son of Arphaxad is the Saleh of Samud. But this opinion seems to be wrong because the tribe (Samud) to which Saleh(as) was sent was a tribe which lived after the time of Saleh, the son of Arphaxad. Some scholars have given the family tree of Samud and Saleh as follows:\nNuh(as)\nJapheth Sham Ham\nArphaxad Iram\nSaleh Jaser\nEber Samud\nPeleg Hadar\nReu Ubaid\nSerug Maseh\nNahor Ubaid\nTerah Saleh(as)\nIbraheem(as)\nIram (Araam) is the same as the name of Sham’s son in the Taurah and Jaser, the son of Iram is also mentioned. But the genealogy described above does not match with that in the Hebrew religious books or Islamic history. That is why nothing definite can be said in this matter. The tribe of Thamud to which Saleh(as) was sent was some tribe which came after the tribe of Aad and built houses carved out of mountains:\n﴿وَاذْكُرُوا إِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَاءَ مِن بَعْدِ عَادٍ وَبَوَّأَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ تَتَّخِذُونَ مِن سُهُولِهَا قُصُورًا وَتَنْحِتُونَ الْجِبَالَ بُيُوتًا ۖ فَاذْكُرُوا آلَاءَ اللَّـهِ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِي الْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ ٧٤﴾\nAnd remember when He made you successors after the 'Aad and settled you in the land, [and] you take for yourselves palaces from its plains and carve from the mountains, homes. Then remember the favors of Allah and do not commit abuse on the earth, spreading corruption.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 74]\nWhatever has been written about the tribe of Thamud cannot be verified as there are no proofs or evidences. But we can definitely say that by the time of the Holy Prophet(saws), no family of the Thamud tribe was left.\nWe also come to know from the Holy Quran that this tribe lived before the time of Musa(as) because in the court of Pharaoh(Firaun), a person who had turned believer warns the king in these words:\n﴿وَقَالَ الَّذِي آمَنَ يَا قَوْمِ إِنِّي أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُم مِّثْلَ يَوْمِ الْأَحْزَابِ ٣٠ مِثْلَ دَأْبِ قَوْمِ نُوحٍ وَعَادٍ وَثَمُودَ وَالَّذِينَ مِن بَعْدِهِمْ ۚ وَمَا اللَّـهُ يُرِيدُ ظُلْمًا لِّلْعِبَادِ ٣١﴾\nAnd he who believed said, \"O my people, indeed I fear for you [a fate] like the day of the companies - Like the custom of the people of Noah and of 'Aad and Thamud and those after them. And Allah wants no injustice for [His] servants.\n[Al-Momin: 30, 31]\nBeyond doubt it was a great tribe which sculpted houses out of mountains.\n(See: Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-81)\nThe author got a chance to see these houses. Looking at them it seems that for every family there was a mountain. According to their needs they had carved out the rooms. The famous ones are the Qasr al-Bint and Diwan. On the doors were drawn pictures of various birds and animals. It appears that these people worshipped these creatures and were very proud of their strength. Allah(swt) sent Saleh(as) to these people to propagate ‘monotheism’ and preach the worship of Allah(swt) alone:\nوَإِلَىٰ ثَمُودَ أَخَاهُمْ صَالِحًا ۗ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۖ\nAnd to the Thamud [We sent] their brother Salih. He said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him.\n[Al-A’raf: 73]\nBut the people of Samud did not listen to him and asked him to show them some sign if he was indeed truthful. (See: Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verse-154)\nIn the form of a sign Allah(swt) sent a she-camel and said:\n﴿إِنَّا مُرْسِلُو النَّاقَةِ فِتْنَةً لَّهُمْ فَارْتَقِبْهُمْ وَاصْطَبِرْ ٢٧﴾\nIndeed, We are sending the she-camel as trial for them, so watch them and be patient.\n[Al-Qamar: 27]\nSaleh(as) said:\n﴿قَالَ هَـٰذِهِ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُومٍ ١٥٥﴾\nHe said, \"This is a she-camel. For her is a [time of] drink, and for you is a [time of] drink, [each] on a known day.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 155]\n﴿وَيَا قَوْمِ هَـٰذِهِ نَاقَةُ اللَّـهِ لَكُمْ آيَةً فَذَرُوهَا تَأْكُلْ فِي أَرْضِ اللَّـهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوءٍ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ قَرِيبٌ ٦٤﴾\n“And O my people, this is the she-camel of Allah - [she is] to you a sign. So let her feed upon Allah 's earth and do not touch her with harm, or you will be taken by an impending punishment.\"\n[Hud: 64]\nBut the people of Samud transgressed and tried to kill the camel:\n﴿فَعَقَرُوا النَّاقَةَ وَعَتَوْا عَنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ وَقَالُوا يَا صَالِحُ ائْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَا إِن كُنتَ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ٧٧﴾\nSo they hamstrung the she-camel and were insolent toward the command of their Lord and said, \"O Salih, bring us what you promise us, if you should be of the messengers.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 77]\n﴿كَذَّبَتْ ثَمُودُ بِطَغْوَاهَا ١١ إِذِ انبَعَثَ أَشْقَاهَا ١٢ فَقَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّـهِ نَاقَةَ اللَّـهِ وَسُقْيَاهَا ١٣ فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَعَقَرُوهَا فَدَمْدَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ رَبُّهُم بِذَنبِهِمْ فَسَوَّاهَا ١٤ وَلَا يَخَافُ عُقْبَاهَا ١٥﴾\nThamud denied [their prophet] by reason of their transgression, When the most wretched of them was sent forth. And the messenger of Allah [Salih] said to them, \"[Do not harm] the she-camel of Allah or [prevent her from] her drink.\"But they denied him and hamstrung her. So their Lord brought down upon them destruction for their sin and made it equal [upon all of them]. And He does not fear the consequence thereof.\n[Ash-Shams: 11-15]\nIn the last verse it has been clarified that neither does Allah(swt) fear nor regret His actions but is All-Powerful. He(swt) is not like the god of the Jews who sometimes regrets his actions as is mentioned in Genesis 6:7 and 8:21.\nThe rest of the story is described in the Holy Quran as under:\n﴿فَعَقَرُوهَا فَقَالَ تَمَتَّعُوا فِي دَارِكُمْ ثَلَاثَةَ أَيَّامٍ ۖ ذَٰلِكَ وَعْدٌ غَيْرُ مَكْذُوبٍ ٦٥ فَلَمَّا جَاءَ أَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا صَالِحًا وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَمِنْ خِزْيِ يَوْمِئِذٍ ۗ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْقَوِيُّ الْعَزِيزُ ٦٦ وَأَخَذَ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَأَصْبَحُوا فِي دِيَارِهِمْ جَاثِمِينَ ٦٧ كَأَن لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيهَا ۗ أَلَا إِنَّ ثَمُودَ كَفَرُوا رَبَّهُمْ ۗ أَلَا بُعْدًا لِّثَمُودَ ٦٨﴾\nBut they hamstrung her, so he said, \"Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days. That is a promise not to be denied.\" So when Our command came, We saved Salih and those who believed with him, by mercy from Us, and [saved them] from the disgrace of that day. Indeed, it is your Lord who is the Powerful, the Exalted in Might. And the shriek seized those who had wronged, and they became within their homes [corpses] fallen prone .As if they had never prospered therein. Unquestionably, Thamud denied their Lord; then, away with Thamud.\n[Hud: 65-68]\nAt another place it says:\n﴿فَأَمَّا ثَمُودُ فَأُهْلِكُوا بِالطَّاغِيَةِ ٥﴾\nSo as for Thamud, they were destroyed by the overpowering [blast].\n[Al-Haqqa: 5]\nIt also says at another place:\n﴿وَأَنَّهُ أَهْلَكَ عَادًا الْأُولَىٰ ٥٠ وَثَمُودَ فَمَا أَبْقَىٰ ٥١﴾\nAnd that He destroyed the first [people of] 'Aad .And Thamud - and He did not spare [them].\n[An-Najm: 50, 51]\nThis is the fate of the people who denied the prophet of Allah(swt), rejected his message and in spite of the clear signs presented by him, did not accept his message. Hence they were wiped out from the face of the earth. When they did not follow the commands of the Creator of this earth, they lost the right to live on His earth and were thus seized in a terrible punishment. It is narrated in the sahih hadith that when the Holy Prophet(saws) went to Tabook, he(saws) would pass through the place of Saleh(as) and some people would enter the houses built by the people of Thamud. The Holy Prophet(saws) would say:\n“These were the people who incurred the wrath of Allah(swt); hence enter their houses crying (as a lesson) lest you be encompassed in His wrath.” (Sahih Bukhari, 3381 and Sahih Muslim, 2980)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that the people got down near the well from which the people of Thamud drank water. They started a fire and started cooking. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know of this he said:\n“Overturn the vessels and feed the dough which you have kneaded to the camels.” Then he(saws) ordered them to move away from there and camp near the well from which the camel of Saleh(as) drank water. He(saws) then said, “Do not go towards the houses of the people who have incurred the wrath of Allah(swt) because I fear lest a calamity befalls you.”\nThat is, these sort of places should not be places of amusement for us; but should be a lesson for us that if we disobey Allah(swt), do not follow His commands, reject the prophets sent by Him and do not tread the path of truth, we also shall face a similar fate. After the calamity, where did Saleh(as) and the other surviving believers go? We do not have any information in this regard either in the Holy Quran or in the sahih hadith. That is why historians have come up with various versions of what followed. Some say that they went away towards Palestine because it was good for their animals. Some others say that they went towards ‘Hajar-maut’ because that was their original place. A grave can be found there which the people say is that of Saleh(as). Some say that all the prophets come to Makkah so that they can worship Allah(swt) in peace and ultimately pass away there itself. In their opinion, at present there are graves of one hundred and twenty prophets there. But this does not seem true because if so, the Holy Prophet(saws) would surely have mentioned the fact and no such mention is made in any of the sahih hadith."],[286,"§Salwa\n‘Salwa’ is a bird like the quail, which Allah(swt) in His infinite mercy had sent for the Bani-Israel when they were roaming the desert of Sina:\nوَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمَامَ وَأَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوَىٰ ۖ كُلُوا مِن طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ ۖ\nAnd We shaded you with clouds and sent down to you manna and quails, [saying], \"Eat from the good things with which We have provided you.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 57] [Al-A’raf: 160] [Ta-Ha: 80]"],[287,"§Samiri\nThe name of ‘Samiri’ occurs three times in the Holy Quran in the Surah-Ta-Ha (See: Verses -85, 87, 95)\nHe was an idolator and a hypocrite who had come with the Bani-Israel to lead them astray. He had learnt some magic tricks and also had some things with him which could produce some unnatural phenomena.\nNow let us take a look at the actions of Samiri.\nWhen Musa(as) went to Mount Tur to receive the Taurah from Allah(swt) and was gone for some time, Samiri started weaving a plot to lead the Bani-Israel astray and Allah(swt) informed Musa(as) about this on Mount Tur:\n﴿قَالَ فَإِنَّا قَدْ فَتَنَّا قَوْمَكَ مِن بَعْدِكَ وَأَضَلَّهُمُ السَّامِرِيُّ ٨٥﴾\n[Allah] said, \"But indeed, We have tried your people after you [departed], and the Samiri has led them astray.\"\n[Ta-Ha: 85]\nThat is, it was a test for the Bani-Israel whether they could stay firm on the path of ‘Tawheed’ or not. How did Samiri lead the Bani-Israel astray?\nHe collected all the gold jewellery of the Bani-Israel which they had brought with them from Egypt and made a calf of gold. He put the dust collected from the footprints of the prophet in its mouth as a result of which a sound started coming out of its mouth. Then Samiri said:\nهَٰذَا إِلَٰهُكُمْ وَإِلَٰهُ مُوسَىٰ\n\"This is your god and the god of Moses.”\n[Ta-Ha: 87-88]\nBut couldn’t they understand that this calf could neither harm nor benefit them in any way. In fact, it could not even answer any of their questions. (See: Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-89)\nHaroon(as) tried his best to stop the Bani-Israel saying that their real God was ‘Rehman.’ He asked them to obey him and follow him, but they refused saying that they would worship the calf till Musa(as) came back. (See: Quran, Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verses-90-91)\nWhen Musa(as) came back and saw the Bani-Israel worshipping the calf, he was furious and in anger threw down the tablets with the commandments of Allah(swt) which he had brought with him from Mount Tur. He then seized Haroon(as) by the head and asked him why he did not stop the Bani-Israel from committing this sin. Haroon(as) said:\nقَالَ ابْنَ أُمَّ إِنَّ الْقَوْمَ اسْتَضْعَفُونِي وَكَادُوا يَقْتُلُونَنِي\n[Aaron] said, \"O son of my mother, indeed the people oppressed me and were about to kill me.”\n[Al-A’raf: 150]\nOne other reason Haroon(as) stated was that if he had been tough then the Bani-Israel would have been scattered and Musa(as) would’ve said:\nإِنِّي خَشِيتُ أَن تَقُولَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِي\n“Indeed, I feared that you would say, 'You caused division among the Children of Israel, and you did not observe [or await] my word.'”\n[Ta-Ha: 94]\nClearly Musa(as) was convinced about the innocence of Haroon(as) because he then turned his attention towards Samiri:\n﴿قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يَا سَامِرِيُّ ٩٥ قَالَ بَصُرْتُ بِمَا لَمْ يَبْصُرُوا بِهِ فَقَبَضْتُ قَبْضَةً مِّنْ أَثَرِ الرَّسُولِ فَنَبَذْتُهَا وَكَذَٰلِكَ سَوَّلَتْ لِي نَفْسِي ٩٦ قَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَإِنَّ لَكَ فِي الْحَيَاةِ أَن تَقُولَ لَا مِسَاسَ ۖ وَإِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّن تُخْلَفَهُ ۖ وَانظُرْ إِلَىٰ إِلَـٰهِكَ الَّذِي ظَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفًا ۖ لَّنُحَرِّقَنَّهُ ثُمَّ لَنَنسِفَنَّهُ فِي الْيَمِّ نَسْفًا ٩٧ إِنَّمَا إِلَـٰهُكُمُ اللَّـهُ الَّذِي لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ وَسِعَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا ٩٨﴾\n[Moses] said, \"And what is your case, O Samiri?\" He said, \"I saw what they did not see, so I took a handful [of dust] from the track of the messenger and threw it, and thus did my soul entice me.\" [Moses] said, \"Then go. And indeed, it is [decreed] for you in [this] life to say, 'No contact.' And indeed, you have an appointment [in the Hereafter] you will not fail to keep. And look at your 'god' to which you remained devoted. We will surely burn it and blow it into the sea with a blast. Your god is only Allah, except for whom there is no deity. He has encompassed all things in knowledge.\"\n[Ta-Ha: 95-98]\nIt is said that then Samiri went away into the forest and started living with the animals and then died there and the corpse was eaten up by the animals."],[288,"§Samuel(as)\nSamuel(as) was the name of a prophet of the Bani-Israel.He is not mentioned by name in the Holy Quran, but the prophet meant in Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-246 of the Holy Quran is Samuel according to many scholars:\nأَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الْمَلَإِ مِن بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ مِن بَعْدِ مُوسَىٰ إِذْ قَالُوا لِنَبِيٍّ لَّهُمُ ابْعَثْ لَنَا مَلِكًا نُّقَاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۖ\nHave you not considered the assembly of the Children of Israel after [the time of] Moses when they said to a prophet of theirs, \"Send to us a king, and we will fight in the way of Allah \"?\nNothing else is mentioned either in the Holy Quran or the sahih hadith about Samuel, but there are two books named after him in the Bible which are in fact one book only. Around 1516 A.D, it was divided into two books. We come to know from them that he was a prophet as well as a judge. He lived in the city of Ramah and travelled to Bethel, Gilgal, Mizpah etc. He built a mosque in Ramah. Once when the Palestines attacked them, he prayed to Allah(swt) along with the people and emerged victorious. (See: 1 Samuel 7:3-14). When he became old the Bani-Israel asked him to choose a successor and he chose a person named ‘Talut’ (Saul) and then the custom of ‘kingship’ started among the Bani-Israel."],[289,"§Satan\n‘Satan’ is the evil spirit which leads men astray. This is not some particular creature, but the evil ones among humans and the jinn have been called satans. The Holy Quran says:\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِيٍّ عَدُوًّا شَيَاطِينَ الْإِنسِ وَالْجِنِّ يُوحِي بَعْضُهُمْ إِلَىٰ بَعْضٍ زُخْرُفَ الْقَوْلِ غُرُورًا\nAnd thus We have made for every prophet an enemy - devils from mankind and jinn, inspiring to one another decorative speech in delusion.\n[Al-An’am: 112]\nWhat is the relation between the humans and the satans? A detailed explanation is given in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith:\n1.Satan is a clear enemy of man and therefore the Holy Quran warns us against following his footsteps. [Al-Baqara: 168-208]\nوَمَن يَتَّبِعْ خُطُوَاتِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَإِنَّهُ يَأْمُرُ بِالْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ ۚ\nAnd whoever follows the footsteps of Satan - indeed, he enjoins immorality and wrongdoing.\n[An-Nur: 21]\n2.Satan calls us towards hell-fire:\n﴿إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ فَاتَّخِذُوهُ عَدُوًّا ۚ إِنَّمَا يَدْعُو حِزْبَهُ لِيَكُونُوا مِنْ أَصْحَابِ السَّعِيرِ ٦﴾\nIndeed, Satan is an enemy to you; so take him as an enemy. He only invites his party to be among the companions of the Blaze.\n[Fatir: 6]\n3.Acts of Satan: All bad actions can be called the acts of Satan; like drinking alcohol, gambling etc. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْأَنصَابُ وَالْأَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَاجْتَنِبُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٩٠﴾\nO you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone alters [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 90]\nSatan scares you with thoughts of poverty so that you do not spend in the way of Allah(swt) and encourages us to engage in immoral acts:\nالشَّيْطَانُ يَعِدُكُمُ الْفَقْرَ وَيَأْمُرُكُم بِالْفَحْشَاءِ\nSatan threatens you with poverty and orders you to immorality.\n[Al-Baqara: 268]\nSatan encourages us to commit acts of disbelief and then deserts us:\n﴿كَمَثَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ إِذْ قَالَ لِلْإِنسَانِ اكْفُرْ فَلَمَّا كَفَرَ قَالَ إِنِّي بَرِيءٌ مِّنكَ إِنِّي أَخَافُ اللَّـهَ رَبَّ الْعَالَمِينَ ١٦﴾\n[The hypocrites are] like the example of Satan when he says to man, \"Disbelieve.\" But when he disbelieves, he says, \"Indeed, I am disassociated from you. Indeed, I fear Allah, Lord of the worlds.\"\n[Al-Hashr: 16]\nSatan not only tries to mislead the Muslims, he does not even spare the disbelievers and deceives them. One such incident occurs in the battle of Badr which is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\nوَإِذْ زَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَعْمَالَهُمْ وَقَالَ لَا غَالِبَ لَكُمُ الْيَوْمَ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَإِنِّي جَارٌ لَّكُمْ ۖ فَلَمَّا تَرَاءَتِ الْفِئَتَانِ نَكَصَ عَلَىٰ عَقِبَيْهِ وَقَالَ إِنِّي بَرِيءٌ مِّنكُمْ إِنِّي أَرَىٰ مَا لَا تَرَوْنَ إِنِّي أَخَافُ اللَّهَ ۚ وَاللَّهُ شَدِيدُ الْعِقَابِ\nAnd [remember] when Satan made their deeds pleasing to them and said, \"No one can overcome you today from among the people, and indeed, I am your protector.\" But when the two armies sighted each other, he turned on his heels and said, \"Indeed, I am disassociated from you. Indeed, I see what you do not see; indeed I fear Allah. And Allah is severe in penalty.\"\n[Al-Anfal: 47]\nInitially the Satan incited the disbelievers of Makkah to wage a war against the Holy Prophet(saws) and the believers of Makkah; but when he saw the angels descending from the heavens for helping the Muslims, he ran away scared. And the disbelievers were left stranded in the battle-field. The satan did not even inform them that the angels had come down for the Muslims so that they could leave the battle-field and at least save their lives. He left the disbelievers in the hands of death and ran away.\nIt is narrated by Ibn-Abbas that in the battle of Badr, a Muslim was chasing a disbeliever when he heard the swishing of a whip. Then he heard the voice of a rider saying, “Go ahead, Haizi'm!” (It may have been the name of the horse). Then, the Muslim saw that the disbeliever was lying on the ground. The man related this incident to the Holy Prophet(saws) and he(saws) replied, ‘You have told the truth. Angels had come down to help from the third heaven.” (Sahih Muslim)\nMany times the satan is engaged in putting misleading thoughts in our minds about Allah(swt). It is narrated by Abu Huraira that Allah(swt)'s Apostle(saws) said, \"Satan comes to one of you and says, 'Who created so-and-so? 'till he says, 'Who has created your Lord?' So, when he inspires such a question, one should seek refuge with Allah(swt) and give up such thoughts.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari:3276)\nTo protect ourselves from the satan, it is necessary to seek the refuge of Allah(swt) at all times. In this regard the Holy Quran says:\n﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِ ١ مَلِكِ النَّاسِ ٢ إِلَـٰهِ النَّاسِ ٣ مِن شَرِّ الْوَسْوَاسِ الْخَنَّاسِ ٤ الَّذِي يُوَسْوِسُ فِي صُدُورِ النَّاسِ ٥ مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ ٦﴾\nSay, \"I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind, The Sovereign of mankind. The God of mankind, From the evil of the retreating whisperer - Who whispers [evil] into the breasts of mankind - From among the jinn and mankind.\"\n[An-Nas: 1-6]\nThis is corroborated in the Sahih hadith also. It is narrated by Abu Zar,\n“I came into the mosque and sat down with the Holy Prophet(saws). He(saws) asked, “Have you offered the namaz?” I replied, “No” so he(saws) said, ‘Go first offer your namaz.’ When I came back after offering namaz, the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “O Abu Zar, seek the refuge of Allah(swt) from the satans among the men and jinn.” I asked, “Are there satans among men?” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “Yes.”\n(Musnad Ahmad 5:258)"],[290,"§Sawaab\n‘Sawaab’ means ‘returns.’ It can either be good or bad. But in the Holy Quran it has only been used to mean ‘reward’. The Holy Quran says:\nوَمَن يُرِدْ ثَوَابَ الدُّنْيَا نُؤْتِهِ مِنْهَا وَمَن يُرِدْ ثَوَابَ الْآخِرَةِ نُؤْتِهِ مِنْهَا ۚ وَسَنَجْزِي الشَّاكِرِينَ\nAnd whoever desires the reward of this world - We will give him thereof; and whoever desires the reward of the Hereafter - We will give him thereof. And we will reward the grateful.\n[Al-i-Imran: 145]\nAddressing the people who haven’t yet turned believers, Allah(swt) says:\n﴿وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا وَاتَّقَوْا لَمَثُوبَةٌ مِّنْ عِندِ اللَّـهِ خَيْرٌ ۖ لَّوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ ١٠٣﴾\nAnd if they had believed and feared Allah, then the reward from Allah would have been [far] better, if they only knew.\n[Al-Baqara: 103]\nWe understand from this that for getting the best reward from Allah(swt), both belief and pious deeds are necessary. Only belief is not sufficient because good deeds are a part of belief without which belief or faith is not complete.\nOne other word has been used in the Holy Quran which means reward and that is ‘Ajr’ or ‘fruit of labour’. It means the wages of a labourer. That is Allah(swt) does not let the deeds of the pious go waste and gives them the reward just as the labourer gets his due wages.\nوَأَنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ\nAllah does not allow the reward of believers to be lost.\n[Al-i-Imran: 171]\nإِنَّا لَا نُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُصْلِحِينَ\nIndeed, We will not allow to be lost the reward of the reformers.\n[Al-A’raf: 170]\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ\nIndeed, Allah does not allow to be lost the reward of the doers of good.\n[At-Tawba: 120]\nBut it is essential that:\n1. Along with true belief, one should also do good deeds.\n(See: Quran, Surah-41, Ha-Meem As-Sajda, Verse-8)\n2. One should be God-fearing and patient. (See: Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-90)\n3. Do not seek rewards from the people of this world but leave it to Allah(swt).\n(See: Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-104)\nWhatever good deeds one does should be solely for seeking the pleasure of Allah(swt). That is why all the messengers made it clear that their message was purely for the pleasure of Allah(swt). They did not seek anything from the people other than to make them follow the right path. It was up to the people to accept or reject their message."],[291,"§Sawamiah\n‘Sawamiah’ is the plural of ‘Soma’a’. This means the monasteries where the Christian monks worship God along with their disciples in solitude. ’Sawamiah’ is mentioned in the Holy Quran in connection with a rule of Allah(swt). Allah(swt) has made a rule for this world that He(swt) checks some people with the help of others. If it hadn’t been so, then the monasteries, churches, synagogues (Jewish prayer houses), mosques in which the name of Allah(swt) is mentioned would have been destroyed and this world would have become a place of chaos and confusion and would have been destroyed before Doomsday. In this regard the Holy Quran says:\n﴿الَّذِينَ أُخْرِجُوا مِن دِيَارِهِم بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ إِلَّا أَن يَقُولُوا رَبُّنَا اللَّـهُ ۗ وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ اللَّـهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُم بِبَعْضٍ لَّهُدِّمَتْ صَوَامِعُ وَبِيَعٌ وَصَلَوَاتٌ وَمَسَاجِدُ يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا اسْمُ اللَّـهِ كَثِيرًا ۗ وَلَيَنصُرَنَّ اللَّـهُ مَن يَنصُرُهُ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَقَوِيٌّ عَزِيزٌ ٤٠﴾\n[They are] those who have been evicted from their homes without right - only because they say, \"Our Lord is Allah.\" And were it not that Allah checks the people, some by means of others, there would have been demolished monasteries, churches, synagogues, and mosques in which the name of Allah is much mentioned. And Allah will surely support those who support Him. Indeed, Allah is Powerful and Exalted in Might.\n[Al-Hajj: 40]"],[292,"§Search for truth\nIt says in the Holy Quran that Allah(swt) will surely guide the person who searches for truth:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا فِينَا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنَا ۚ وَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَمَعَ الْمُحْسِنِينَ ٦٩﴾\nAnd those who strive for Us - We will surely guide them to Our ways. And indeed, Allah is with the doers of good.\n[Al-Ankaboot: 69]\nWe relate here a story from Islamic history in which a man sets out in quest of truth and in spite of many difficulties and hurdles, finally attains his goal. The story is told in the first person.\nI was from Iran. My father was the caretaker of a temple and following his order I would light the fire in the temple and would try to always keep it burning. My father loved me a lot because of this. So much so that he never let me out of the house. One day I came out of the house to do some work for my father and after walking some distance I heard the church-bells ringing. I was surprised by the sound which I had never heard till then. I went to the church and listened to the prayers going on there and was there till evening. Then I came home. My father asked me the reason for the delay and I told him that I had gone to the church and liked the prayers going on there. As soon as I said this, my father tied me up with iron chains and said that your religion is better than theirs. But I found Christianity better. So I sent a message to the padre that I wanted to learn more about Christianity. He replied that I should go to Syria where there was a big church and I could get more knowledge. I asked him to inform me when some caravan came from Syria. That day came and breaking free of the shackles, I went away to Syria. There I presented myself to the great priest and started serving him. But I found that he was an evil man. He would take donations but did not spend them on the poor and stored them away. When he died and people came to bury him I told them the truth. When they asked for proof I took them to the vault where he had hidden gold and silver. The people were furious and hanged and stoned him. Then another priest was appointed. The new man was very pious. He did not desire this world but strived for success in the Hereafter. I started serving him. When he was on his death-bed I told him, “O Padre! You know how much I love you. You are about to leave this world. What should I do and where should I go?”. He replied, “O son! People have changed. Today I do not know any padre who lives the way I do. But yes there is a padre in Iraq. Go to him, you will see that he is like me.” After the death of the priest, I went away to Iraq and told the padre there the purpose of my coming. He was very happy and kept me in his service. I found him to be very pious like the previous padre. When the time of his death drew near I told him, “O respected padre! Your end is near. Tell me where should I go?”. He replied, “O son! I do not know anybody who is like us. But go to Nusaybin.” After the death of the padre I went to Nusaybin and told my story to the priest. He was very happy and allowed me to stay with him. When he was about to die, I asked him, “O padre! where should I go?” He replied, “Go to Bamorion. You will find that the padre there is just like us.” After his death I went to Bamorion and started living there. I started doing business and became the owner of many cows. When the priest there was on his death-bed, I asked him, “O padre! I have told you my story. Where should I go now?” He replied, “O son! I do not know of any person on this earth to whom I can advise you to go. But listen carefully to what I say. It is now time for the prophet to come who shall follow the religion of Ibraheem(as) and who will be born in Arabia. Then he shall migrate to a place which will be full of date palms. Few of his signs are that he will accept gifts but not charity. He will have the seal of prophethood between his shoulders. If you can travel to this place go there and search for him.” The priest died after that.\nAfter the death of the priest, I stayed for some time in Bamorion. Then I came to know that a few traders had come from Arabia. I met them and asked them to take me with them in exchange for the cows and goats which I had. They agreed but when we reached the valley of Qura (which is between Syria and Madina) they sold me to a Jew. I started staying with the Jew. That place was full of date palms. I started wondering if it was the same place about which I had been told. Then, the Jew’s cousin came there and bought me and took me with him to Madina. As soon as I saw Madina, my eyes lit up and I was convinced that this was the place which had been described to me. I started living the life of a slave and I got very little time after doing my master’s tasks.\nOne day I heard my master’s cousin telling him,”Have you heard that a person has come to Quba from Makkah who says that he is a prophet?” Hearing this I trembled with excitement. I asked him to repeat what he was saying. Hearing this my master scolded me not to listen to these things and to do my work.\nOne day, after dark I went to the prophet(saws) and said, “You and your companions have migrated and come to this place. You must be needy. Please accept this charity of whatever I have.” Saying this I put a few eatables in front of him. The Prophet(saws) said to his companions, “You eat these things.” As for himself he took away his hand and did not eat any of the things. I said to myself that the first sign has been proved that he(saws) does not take charity. Then, after he(saws) entered Madina, I once more came to him and said, “I have seen that you do not take charity. So, I have brought a gift for you.” So, he (saws) accepted the gift, ate some of it and gave some of it to his companions. I said to myself that the second sign also has proved true that he(saws) accepts gifts.\nThen one day I went to meet him when he(saws) had buried someone in Baqi and was sitting there. He(saws) was wrapped in two shawls. I said Salam to him and started searching his back. He(saws) removed the shawl from his back. As soon as I saw the seal of prophethood on his back, I kissed it and hugging him started weeping. Lovingly he(saws) made me sit with him and asked me, “What is the matter? Tell me.” I told him my story from the beginning and the troubles I had undergone in search of him. I consider myself extremely lucky that Allah(swt) has guided me to the truth.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) and his companions were very impressed with this story.\nThis was the story of Hazrat Salman Pharsi(ra) who was freed by the efforts of the Holy Prophet(saws). He gained prominence in Islam.\nSomeone has rightly said,”The one who tries will definitely find the truth.”"],[293,"§Shaheed\n‘Shaheed’ is one of the attributes of Allah(swt) which means: witness. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿قُلْ يَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ لِمَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِآيَاتِ اللَّـهِ وَاللَّـهُ شَهِيدٌ عَلَىٰ مَا تَعْمَلُونَ ٩٨﴾\nSay, \"O People of the Scripture, why do you disbelieve in the verses of Allah while Allah is Witness over what you do?\"\n[Al-i-Imran: 98]\nAnd in the same sense this word has been used for people also. For instance, the Holy Quran says about the Holy Prophet(saws):\n﴿فَكَيْفَ إِذَا جِئْنَا مِن كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ بِشَهِيدٍ وَجِئْنَا بِكَ عَلَىٰ هَـٰؤُلَاءِ شَهِيدًا ٤١﴾\nSo how [will it be] when We bring from every nation a witness and we bring you, [O Muhammad] against these [people] as a witness?\n[An-Nisa: 41]\nThat is, every prophet will be witness to the fact that he has delivered the message of Allah(swt) to his people. After that, if the people did not pay heed then it is not the fault of the messengers. In the same way, the Holy Prophet(saws) will be made a witness against the disbelievers of Makkah and will give evidence that O Allah(swt)! These people have rejected your message.\nSome commentators have written that the Holy Prophet(saws) will be a witness for other prophets that they have indeed delivered the message of Allah(swt) to their respective tribes but that those people did not believe.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) gained this knowledge from the Holy Quran in which detailed stories of various prophets have been explained. It will be a very tough period when the Holy Prophet(saws) will be brought forth as witness. That is why, when the Holy Prophet(saws) asked Abdullah-bin-Masood to recite the Holy Quran and he came to this verse, the Holy Prophet(saws) asked him to stop.\nIt is narrated by Abdullah-bin-Masood that he looked towards the Holy Prophet(saws) and saw tears flowing out of his eyes. (Sahih Bukhari, 4582)\nOne other meaning of ‘Shaheed’ is ‘one who is martyred in the path of Allah(swt)’ whose plural is ‘Shuhda’ as it says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَمَن يُطِعِ اللَّـهَ وَالرَّسُولَ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ مَعَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمَ اللَّـهُ عَلَيْهِم مِّنَ النَّبِيِّينَ وَالصِّدِّيقِينَ وَالشُّهَدَاءِ وَالصَّالِحِينَ ۚ وَحَسُنَ أُولَـٰئِكَ رَفِيقًا ٦٩﴾\nAnd whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger - those will be with the ones upon whom Allah has bestowed favor of the prophets, the steadfast affirmers of truth, the martyrs and the righteous. And excellent are those as companions.\n[An-Nisa: 69]\nAt another place in the Holy Quran it says:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِاللَّـهِ وَرُسُلِهِ أُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الصِّدِّيقُونَ ۖ وَالشُّهَدَاءُ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ لَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ وَنُورُهُمْ ۖ وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَكَذَّبُوا بِآيَاتِنَا أُولَـٰئِكَ أَصْحَابُ الْجَحِيمِ ١٩﴾\nAnd those who have believed in Allah and His messengers - those are [in the ranks of] the supporters of truth and the martyrs, with their Lord. For them is their reward and their light. But those who have disbelieved and denied Our verses - those are the companions of Hellfire.\n[Al-Hadid: 19]\nThat is, the truthful and the martyrs will enter paradise in the light of their deeds. One great speciality of these people is that they are alive with their Lord:\n﴿وَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ أَمْوَاتًا ۚ بَلْ أَحْيَاءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ ١٦٩﴾\nAnd never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, receiving provision.\n[Al-i-Imran: 169]\n﴿وَلَا تَقُولُوا لِمَن يُقْتَلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ أَمْوَاتٌ ۚ بَلْ أَحْيَاءٌ وَلَـٰكِن لَّا تَشْعُرُونَ ١٥٤﴾\nAnd do not say about those who are killed in the way of Allah, \"They are dead.\" Rather, they are alive, but you perceive [it] not.\n[Al-Baqara: 154]\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ هَاجَرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ ثُمَّ قُتِلُوا أَوْ مَاتُوا لَيَرْزُقَنَّهُمُ اللَّـهُ رِزْقًا حَسَنًا ۚ وَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَهُوَ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِينَ ٥٨ لَيُدْخِلَنَّهُم مُّدْخَلًا يَرْضَوْنَهُ ۗ وَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَعَلِيمٌ حَلِيمٌ ٥٩﴾\nAnd those who emigrated for the cause of Allah and then were killed or died - Allah will surely provide for them a good provision. And indeed, it is Allah who is the best of providers. He will surely cause them to enter an entrance with which they will be pleased, and indeed, Allah is Knowing and Forbearing.\n[Al-Hajj: 58, 59]\nThat is the reason why a martyr is neither given the funereal bath, nor shrouded in cloth nor is the funeral salah offered for him because the funeral salah is offered for the dead and not for the living.\nThe excellence of a martyr:\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith by Anas(ra) that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Any person who enters the paradise will never want to come back to earth even if the whole world and all that is in it is offered to him except for a martyr who, seeing the merits of martyrdom will want to come back to earth so that he can die ten times in the path of Allah(swt).”\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that seeing the honour granted to him in paradise, he will wish to come back and die ten times in the path of Allah(swt).\n(Sahih Bukhari, 2817 and Sahih Muslim, 1877)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Were it not for fear that it would be difficult for my followers, I would not have remained behind any army units going on jihad. No doubt I wish I could fight in Allah(swt)'s path and become shahid(die in the way of Allah(swt)) and come to life and become shahid again, come to life again and again become shahid.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 36 and Sahih Muslim, 1876)\nTypes of shaheed:\nThe qualification of ‘shaheed’ is also given for various reasons to people who have died in other ways:\n1. People who have died in plague.\n2. People who die due to stomach ailments.\n3. People who die due to drowning in water.\n4. People who die due to something falling.\n5. People who die in the way of Allah(swt) (See: Sahih Muslim, 1914 and Sahih Bukhari, 652)\n6. People who die protecting their wealth.\n7. People who die protecting their families.\n8. People who die protecting their religion. (See: Abu Dawood, 4772 and Tirmizi, 1455)\n9. People who die in fires.\n10. Pregnant women who die.\n11. People who die due to rupturing of some internal wounds or cancer. (which is called ‘Zatuljamb’ in Arabic)\n12. People who die in accidents.\n13. People who die in communal riots. (See: Abu-Dawood, 3111 and Nasai, 3194 and Ibn-Majah, 2803)\nAll the above mentioned people are also called ‘shaheed’. But the best are those who sacrifice their lives in the path of Allah(swt). That is why the rules and commands related to ‘shaheed’ are applicable only to the martyrs dying in the way of Allah(swt). In the case of the other ‘shaheed’ also there are various levels with Allah(swt)."],[294,"§Shahvat\n‘Shahvat’ means wish or desire as:\nوَلَكُمْ فِيهَا مَا تَشْتَهِي أَنفُسُكُمْ\nAnd you will have therein whatever your souls desire.\n[Ha-Meem As-Sajda: 31]\n﴿وَأَمْدَدْنَاهُم بِفَاكِهَةٍ وَلَحْمٍ مِّمَّا يَشْتَهُونَ ٢٢﴾\nAnd We will provide them with fruit and meat from whatever they desire.\n[At-Tur: 22]\nBut in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith, the word has been used for physical pleasures.\n﴿زُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ الشَّهَوَاتِ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ وَالْبَنِينَ وَالْقَنَاطِيرِ الْمُقَنطَرَةِ مِنَ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ وَالْخَيْلِ الْمُسَوَّمَةِ وَالْأَنْعَامِ وَالْحَرْثِ ۗ ذَٰلِكَ مَتَاعُ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا ۖ وَاللَّـهُ عِندَهُ حُسْنُ الْمَآبِ ١٤﴾\nBeautified for people is the love of that which they desire - of women and sons, heaped-up sums of gold and silver, fine branded horses, and cattle and tilled land. That is the enjoyment of worldly life, but Allah has with Him the best return.\n[Al-i-Imran: 14]\n﴿إِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ شَهْوَةً مِّن دُونِ النِّسَاءِ ۚ بَلْ أَنتُمْ قَوْمٌ مُّسْرِفُونَ ٨١﴾\n“Indeed, you approach men with desire, instead of women. Rather, you are a transgressing people.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 81]\nAfter describing the prophets, the following people have been mentioned:\n﴿فَخَلَفَ مِن بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ أَضَاعُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَاتَّبَعُوا الشَّهَوَاتِ ۖ فَسَوْفَ يَلْقَوْنَ غَيًّا ٥٩﴾\nBut there came after them successors who neglected prayer and pursued desires; so they are going to meet evil.\n[Maryam: 59]\n﴿وَاللَّـهُ يُرِيدُ أَن يَتُوبَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَيُرِيدُ الَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ الشَّهَوَاتِ أَن تَمِيلُوا مَيْلًا عَظِيمًا ٢٧﴾\nAllah wants to accept your repentance, but those who follow [their] passions want you to digress [into] a great deviation.\n[An-Nisa: 27]\nEven in the divine books revealed before the Holy Quran, ‘shahvat’ has been criticized as this is the main cause of men falling into sin. (Bible- Jacob 1:14-15)\nBut unlike in the other religions, the roots of desires are not cut off in Islam, but to balance them it has been commanded to get married. And furthermore by forbidding the evil things like dancing, singing, consuming alcohol etc, which incite desires, they have been taken care of."],[295,"§Sheba\n‘Sheba’ was an Arabian tribe who lived in Yemen.\nThese people have been described in the eighth century ruins of the Ashurites. In the Bible they have sometimes been called the descendants of Cush who was the son of Ham and the grandson of Nuh(as) and sometimes the descendants of Yakshan, the son of Ibraheem(as) and Keturah. But how did these people who lived in Syria which is to the north of Arabia come to Yemen which is to the south of Arabia? The answer is that they were nomads and did not have a fixed place of living. So, wandering, they came to the south of Arabia. They fought with the weak kings ruling there, triumphed over them and established themselves there. That is why when the Abyssinian rulers attacked Yemen, these people again fled to Syria and established their kingdom there.\nWhen Sulaiman(as) did not see the bird Hud-hud, he was furious and said, “I shall punish it severely or kill it.”\n﴿فَمَكَثَ غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍ فَقَالَ أَحَطتُ بِمَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهِ وَجِئْتُكَ مِن سَبَإٍ بِنَبَإٍ يَقِينٍ ٢٢﴾\nBut the hoopoe stayed not long and said, \"I have encompassed [in knowledge] that which you have not encompassed, and I have come to you from Sheba with certain news.\n[An-Naml: 22]\nAt another place ‘Sheba’ has been described as follows:\n﴿لَقَدْ كَانَ لِسَبَإٍ فِي مَسْكَنِهِمْ آيَةٌ ۖ جَنَّتَانِ عَن يَمِينٍ وَشِمَالٍ ۖ كُلُوا مِن رِّزْقِ رَبِّكُمْ وَاشْكُرُوا لَهُ ۚ بَلْدَةٌ طَيِّبَةٌ وَرَبٌّ غَفُورٌ ١٥﴾\nThere was for [the tribe of] Saba' in their dwelling place a sign: two [fields of] gardens on the right and on the left. [They were told], \"Eat from the provisions of your Lord and be grateful to Him. A good land [have you], and a forgiving Lord.\"\n[Saba: 15]\nIn the above verse, gardens on the right and left could also mean that wherever one looked, to the right or left, one could see pleasant greenery.\nNow let us describe the tribe of Sheba here:\nThe tribe of Sheba inhabited Yemen. They lived during the 9th century B.C. According to the Holy Quran, this tribe is first mentioned around 926-965 B.C. Its ruler was a queen whose name according to the Arabic books was Bilquis, but no name is mentioned either in the Bible or the Holy Quran or the sahih hadith. In the books of commentary the name Bilquis is mentioned but this does not prove anything. This tribe was prosperous for some ten years. Then in the first century B.C, another Arabic tribe named Himyar displaced them and established their kingdom. We come to know from the Bible that the people of Sheba traded in spices, precious stones and gold (See: Ezekiel 27:22) Their trade routes went from Arabia to India to Abyssinia. They have been mentioned many times in the Bible (See: Job, 1:15, 6:19; Genesis 10:7; Joel, 3:8; Jeremiah, 6:20), but they haven’t been mentioned in the descriptions in the Holy Quran. The scholars of Greece and Rome have described them in detail in the third century B.C because from the time of Sulaiman(as), this tribe had gained prominence as a very wealthy tribe. The sun and the moon were their gods. It is mentioned in Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-24 that they worshipped the sun. We come to know the same thing from the Arabic books also. The people of Sheba considered themselves to be from the sun-dynasty. In the excavations of Yemen, many ruins of a temple were found in which many idols of a god called Almakha and various signs of his worship were found. But when the wrath of Allah(swt) descended upon this tribe, they were totally wiped out from the face of this earth as Allah(swt) is not pleased with any polytheistic tribe. However much they prosper in this world, a day will surely come when they shall be destroyed. It is said that the people of Sheba ate from golden and silver vessels. They had works of gold, silver and ivory in their homes and hearing these tales the Greek and Romans were excited. This was the reason the Abyssinian king attacked the tribe again and again to usurp their kingdom. It is said that they built a splendid palace on the high mountains of San’aa which was called ‘Gumdaan’ and which is one of the wonders of the world. Around 650 B.C, they built a dam in Maarib which was between many mountains. And the later kings kept building it further. After the dam was completed, they made Maarib which is about 96 kilometers from San’aa their capital. Then later on they left Maarib and made Zaidan their capital which in turn became famous as Ziphar and is now a part of Oman.\nThen, the downfall of this tribe started in 300 B.C. They incurred huge losses in trade. There started group fights and riots. There was no peace in the country. So much so that the Abyssinian kings triumphed over them. After a great struggle they gained freedom. Around 450 B.C, Allah(swt) sent the flood of the dam and the whole kingdom was submerged in water. All the farms were destroyed.\nWhen the atrocities of the Jewish kings became too much, the Abyssinian king who was a Christian once again conquered Yemen. In order to gain control over the entire Arab region, his Abyssinian viceroy set forth towards Makkah in 570 A.D with a huge army of elephants and planned to attack the Holy Kaaba. But Allah(swt) destroyed them with the help of flocks of birds who rained pebbles made of clay on them. The army was destroyed. The Surah-Feel of the Holy Quran refers to this incident. Then in 575 A.D, Yemen was conquered by the Iranians. And in 628 A.D, when the Iranian governor became a Muslim, Yemen became a Muslim state.\nAfter this brief history of Yemen, let us once more come back to the tribe of Sheba:\nFrom the description in the Holy Quran we come to know that the tribe of Sheba was a very great tribe of its time and that their capital was Sana’a. Their main occupations were trade and agriculture. They had built a huge dam between mountains to stock rain water. The word ‘Arim’ is used for this dam in the Holy Quran [Saba: 16]. They used this water for agriculture and as a result there was greenery everywhere. They should have been grateful to Allah(swt) and worshipped Him in all humility, but instead they left the path of Allah(swt) and turned rebellious. They arrogantly thought that their prosperity was solely due to their own efforts. As a result they incurred the wrath of Allah(swt) and as a punishment, Allah(swt) broke the dam:\n﴿فَأَعْرَضُوا فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَيْلَ الْعَرِمِ وَبَدَّلْنَاهُم بِجَنَّتَيْهِمْ جَنَّتَيْنِ ذَوَاتَيْ أُكُلٍ خَمْطٍ وَأَثْلٍ وَشَيْءٍ مِّن سِدْرٍ قَلِيلٍ ١٦ ذَٰلِكَ جَزَيْنَاهُم بِمَا كَفَرُوا ۖ وَهَلْ نُجَازِي إِلَّا الْكَفُورَ ١٧﴾\nBut they turned away [refusing], so We sent upon them the flood of the dam, and We replaced their two [fields of] gardens with gardens of bitter fruit, tamarisks and something of sparse lote trees. [By] that We repaid them because they disbelieved. And do We [thus] repay except the ungrateful?\n[Saba: 16, 17]\nThat is, when they disbelieved and rejected Our commands, We broke the dam and destroyed their farms. All their fine crops were destroyed and in their place wild fruits and flowers came up and they had to subsist on those."],[296,"§Sheba, Queen of\n‘Sheba’ was a tribe of Yemen. (See ‘Sheba’). During the time of Sulaiman(as), a queen ruled over this tribe. Her name is not known, but according to the Arabic books, it was ‘Bilquis.’ In the Holy Quran and the Bible, a detailed description is given from which we come to know that she went to Baitul-Muqaddas to meet Sulaiman(as). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَتَفَقَّدَ الطَّيْرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِيَ لَا أَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ أَمْ كَانَ مِنَ الْغَائِبِينَ ٢٠﴾\nAnd he took attendance of the birds and said, \"Why do I not see the hoopoe - or is he among the absent?\n[An-Naml: 20]\n﴿لَأُعَذِّبَنَّهُ عَذَابًا شَدِيدًا أَوْ لَأَذْبَحَنَّهُ أَوْ لَيَأْتِيَنِّي بِسُلْطَانٍ مُّبِينٍ ٢١ فَمَكَثَ غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍ فَقَالَ أَحَطتُ بِمَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهِ وَجِئْتُكَ مِن سَبَإٍ بِنَبَإٍ يَقِينٍ ٢٢ إِنِّي وَجَدتُّ امْرَأَةً تَمْلِكُهُمْ وَأُوتِيَتْ مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيمٌ ٢٣ وَجَدتُّهَا وَقَوْمَهَا يَسْجُدُونَ لِلشَّمْسِ مِن دُونِ اللَّـهِ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَعْمَالَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّبِيلِ فَهُمْ لَا يَهْتَدُونَ ٢٤ أَلَّا يَسْجُدُوا لِلَّـهِ الَّذِي يُخْرِجُ الْخَبْءَ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُخْفُونَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُونَ ٢٥ اللَّـهُ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيمِ ۩ ٢٦ قَالَ سَنَنظُرُ أَصَدَقْتَ أَمْ كُنتَ مِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ ٢٧ اذْهَب بِّكِتَابِي هَـٰذَا فَأَلْقِهْ إِلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَانظُرْ مَاذَا يَرْجِعُونَ ٢٨ قَالَتْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ إِنِّي أُلْقِيَ إِلَيَّ كِتَابٌ كَرِيمٌ ٢٩ إِنَّهُ مِن سُلَيْمَانَ وَإِنَّهُ بِسْمِ اللَّـهِ الرَّحْمَـٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ ٣٠ أَلَّا تَعْلُوا عَلَيَّ وَأْتُونِي مُسْلِمِينَ ٣١ قَالَتْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ أَفْتُونِي فِي أَمْرِي مَا كُنتُ قَاطِعَةً أَمْرًا حَتَّىٰ تَشْهَدُونِ ٣٢ قَالُوا نَحْنُ أُولُو قُوَّةٍ وَأُولُو بَأْسٍ شَدِيدٍ وَالْأَمْرُ إِلَيْكِ فَانظُرِي مَاذَا تَأْمُرِينَ ٣٣ قَالَتْ إِنَّ الْمُلُوكَ إِذَا دَخَلُوا قَرْيَةً أَفْسَدُوهَا وَجَعَلُوا أَعِزَّةَ أَهْلِهَا أَذِلَّةً ۖ وَكَذَٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُونَ ٣٤ وَإِنِّي مُرْسِلَةٌ إِلَيْهِم بِهَدِيَّةٍ فَنَاظِرَةٌ بِمَ يَرْجِعُ الْمُرْسَلُونَ ٣٥ فَلَمَّا جَاءَ سُلَيْمَانَ قَالَ أَتُمِدُّونَنِ بِمَالٍ فَمَا آتَانِيَ اللَّـهُ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّا آتَاكُم بَلْ أَنتُم بِهَدِيَّتِكُمْ تَفْرَحُونَ ٣٦ ارْجِعْ إِلَيْهِمْ فَلَنَأْتِيَنَّهُم بِجُنُودٍ لَّا قِبَلَ لَهُم بِهَا وَلَنُخْرِجَنَّهُم مِّنْهَا أَذِلَّةً وَهُمْ صَاغِرُونَ ٣٧ قَالَ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ أَيُّكُمْ يَأْتِينِي بِعَرْشِهَا قَبْلَ أَن يَأْتُونِي مُسْلِمِينَ ٣٨ قَالَ عِفْرِيتٌ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ أَنَا آتِيكَ بِهِ قَبْلَ أَن تَقُومَ مِن مَّقَامِكَ ۖ وَإِنِّي عَلَيْهِ لَقَوِيٌّ أَمِينٌ ٣٩ قَالَ الَّذِي عِندَهُ عِلْمٌ مِّنَ الْكِتَابِ أَنَا آتِيكَ بِهِ قَبْلَ أَن يَرْتَدَّ إِلَيْكَ طَرْفُكَ ۚ فَلَمَّا رَآهُ مُسْتَقِرًّا عِندَهُ قَالَ هَـٰذَا مِن فَضْلِ رَبِّي لِيَبْلُوَنِي أَأَشْكُرُ أَمْ أَكْفُرُ ۖ وَمَن شَكَرَ فَإِنَّمَا يَشْكُرُ لِنَفْسِهِ ۖ وَمَن كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ رَبِّي غَنِيٌّ كَرِيمٌ ٤٠ قَالَ نَكِّرُوا لَهَا عَرْشَهَا نَنظُرْ أَتَهْتَدِي أَمْ تَكُونُ مِنَ الَّذِينَ لَا يَهْتَدُونَ ٤١ فَلَمَّا جَاءَتْ قِيلَ أَهَـٰكَذَا عَرْشُكِ ۖ قَالَتْ كَأَنَّهُ هُوَ ۚ وَأُوتِينَا الْعِلْمَ مِن قَبْلِهَا وَكُنَّا مُسْلِمِينَ ٤٢ وَصَدَّهَا مَا كَانَت تَّعْبُدُ مِن دُونِ اللَّـهِ ۖ إِنَّهَا كَانَتْ مِن قَوْمٍ كَافِرِينَ ٤٣ قِيلَ لَهَا ادْخُلِي الصَّرْحَ ۖ فَلَمَّا رَأَتْهُ حَسِبَتْهُ لُجَّةً وَكَشَفَتْ عَن سَاقَيْهَا ۚ قَالَ إِنَّهُ صَرْحٌ مُّمَرَّدٌ مِّن قَوَارِيرَ ۗ قَالَتْ رَبِّ إِنِّي ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِي وَأَسْلَمْتُ مَعَ سُلَيْمَانَ لِلَّـهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٤٤﴾\nI will surely punish him with a severe punishment or slaughter him unless he brings me clear authorization.\" But the hoopoe stayed not long and said, \"I have encompassed [in knowledge] that which you have not encompassed, and I have come to you from Sheba with certain news. Indeed, I found [there] a woman ruling them, and she has been given of all things, and she has a great throne. I found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allah, and Satan has made their deeds pleasing to them and averted them from [His] way, so they are not guided, [And] so they do not prostrate to Allah, who brings forth what is hidden within the heavens and the earth and knows what you conceal and what you declare - Allah - there is no deity except Him, Lord of the Great Throne.\" [Solomon] said, \"We will see whether you were truthful or were of the liars. Take this letter of mine and deliver it to them. Then leave them and see what [answer] they will return.\" She said, \"O eminent ones, indeed, to me has been delivered a noble letter. Indeed, it is from Solomon, and indeed, it reads: 'In the name of Allah, the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful, Be not haughty with me but come to me in submission [as Muslims].' \" She said, \"O eminent ones, advise me in my affair. I would not decide a matter until you witness [for] me.\" They said, \"We are men of strength and of great military might, but the command is yours, so see what you will command.\" She said, \"Indeed kings - when they enter a city, they ruin it and render the honored of its people humbled. And thus do they do. But indeed, I will send to them a gift and see with what [reply] the messengers will return.\" So when they came to Solomon, he said, \"Do you provide me with wealth? But what Allah has given me is better than what He has given you. Rather, it is you who rejoice in your gift. Return to them, for we will surely come to them with soldiers that they will be powerless to encounter, and we will surely expel them therefrom in humiliation, and they will be debased.\" [Solomon] said, \"O assembly [of jinn], which of you will bring me her throne before they come to me in submission?\" A powerful one from among the jinn said, \"I will bring it to you before you rise from your place, and indeed, I am for this [task] strong and trustworthy.\" Said one who had knowledge from the Scripture, \"I will bring it to you before your glance returns to you.\" And when [Solomon] saw it placed before him, he said, \"This is from the favor of my Lord to test me whether I will be grateful or ungrateful. And whoever is grateful - his gratitude is only for [the benefit of] himself. And whoever is ungrateful - then indeed, my Lord is Free of need and Generous.\" He said, \"Disguise for her her throne; we will see whether she will be guided [to truth] or will be of those who is not guided.\" So when she arrived, it was said [to her], \"Is your throne like this?\" She said, \"[It is] as though it was it.\" [Solomon said], \"And we were given knowledge before her, and we have been Muslims [in submission to Allah]. And that which she was worshipping other than Allah had averted her [from submission to Him]. Indeed, she was from a disbelieving people.\" She was told, \"Enter the palace.\" But when she saw it, she thought it was a body of water and uncovered her shins [to wade through]. He said, \"Indeed, it is a palace [whose floor is] made smooth with glass.\" She said, \"My Lord, indeed I have wronged myself, and I submit with Solomon to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\"\n[An-Naml: 21-44]\nThe gist of the above verses is that the tribe of Sheba was worshipping the sun. Sulaiman(as) started the letter addressed to the Queen of Sheba with the name of Allah(swt) so that the sun-worship could be condemned. It was one of the miracles given to Sulaiman(as) by Allah(swt) that the jinn which were in his service could bring the throne of the Queen of Sheba in a split second from Yemen to Baitul-Muqaddas. This proves the Might of Allah(swt). The gods and goddesses which she and her people were worshipping had prevented her from true belief. But then she realizes her folly and becomes a Muslim.\nIn the Holy Quran, the story of the Queen of Sheba is not given as a historical event but to preach ‘monotheism’ or ‘Tawheed’ and condemn ‘polytheism’.\nBut the way it has been described in the Bible does not throw light on any particular point of instruction.\nThe Queen of Sheba visits Solomon:\n1. When the queen of Sheba heard about the fame of Solomon and his relationship to the Lord, she came to test Solomon with hard questions.\n2 Arriving at Jerusalem with a very great caravan—with camels carrying spices, large quantities of gold, and precious stones—she came to Solomon and talked with him about all that she had on her mind.\n3 Solomon answered all her questions; nothing was too hard for the king to explain to her.\n4 When the queen of Sheba saw all the wisdom of Solomon and the palace he had built,\n5 the food on his table, the seating of his officials, the attending servants in their robes, his cupbearers, and the burnt offerings he made at the temple of the Lord, she was overwhelmed.\n6 She said to the king, “The report I heard in my own country about your achievements and your wisdom is true.\n7 But I did not believe these things until I came and saw with my own eyes. Indeed, not even half was told me; in wisdom and wealth you have far exceeded the report I heard.\n8 How happy your people must be! How happy your officials, who continually stand before you and hear your wisdom!\n9 Praise be to the Lord your God, who has delighted in you and placed you on the throne of Israel. Because of the Lord’s eternal love for Israel, he has made you king to maintain justice and righteousness.”\n10 And she gave the king 120 talents of gold, large quantities of spices, and precious stones. Never again were so many spices brought in as those the queen of Sheba gave to King Solomon.\n11 (Hiram’s ships brought gold from Ophir; and from there they brought great cargoes of almugwood and precious stones.\n12 The king used the almugwood to make supports for the temple of the Lord and for the royal palace, and to make harps and lyres for the musicians. So much almugwood has never been imported or seen since that day.)\n13 King Solomon gave the queen of Sheba all she desired and asked for, besides what he had given her out of his royal bounty. Then she left and returned with her retinue to her own country.\n(See: Bible 1 Kings 10:1-13)\nWe do not come to know from the Holy Quran, the sahih hadith or the Bible whether Sulaiman(as) married the Queen of Sheba or not but we come to know from Abyssinian history that the kings of Abyssinia were the descendants of the sons of Sulaiman(as) and the Queen of Sheba. That is why Jews do not consider the Abyssinian Jews to be the descendants of Bani-Israel as the Queen of Sheba was not from the Bani-Israel."],[297,"§Shiara\n‘Shiara’(Sirius) is the name of a star which is seen during summer. The Arabian tribe Banu-Khuza’a worshipped this star. They sacrificed animals in its name. They invoked this star and sought favours from it when in fact Allah(swt) is the Creator of this star as well as of the entire Creation. The Holy Quran says about this:\n﴿وَأَنَّهُ هُوَ رَبُّ الشِّعْرَىٰ ٤٩﴾\nAnd that it is He who is the Lord of Sirius.\n[An-Najm: 49]\nThat is, just as Allah(swt) is the Lord of the entire universe, He(swt) is the Lord of the star Sirius also. So, how can people worship it?"],[298,"§Shirk\nAllah(swt) has created man with the inherent attribute of ‘monotheism’. But as time went on, the belief in monotheism became weak and ‘polytheism’ or ‘shirk’ crept in. Then, Allah(swt) used various means to remind man about his basic nature and warn him about the harmful effects of shirk so that on the Day of Judgement man cannot say that he wasn’t warned or guided. Of the various ways of guidance a few are:\n1. The sending of messengers or prophets:\n﴿يَا مَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنسِ أَلَمْ يَأْتِكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنكُمْ يَقُصُّونَ عَلَيْكُمْ آيَاتِي وَيُنذِرُونَكُمْ لِقَاءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هَـٰذَا ۚ قَالُوا شَهِدْنَا عَلَىٰ أَنفُسِنَا ۖ وَغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا وَشَهِدُوا عَلَىٰ أَنفُسِهِمْ أَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا كَافِرِينَ ١٣٠﴾\n\"O company of jinn and mankind, did there not come to you messengers from among you, relating to you My verses and warning you of the meeting of this Day of yours?\" They will say, \"We bear witness against ourselves\"; and the worldly life had deluded them, and they will bear witness against themselves that they were disbelievers.\n[Al-An’am: 130]\nثُمَّ أَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا تَتْرَىٰ\nThen We sent Our messengers in succession.\n[Al-Mu’minun: 44]\nThese messengers reminded the people what they had forgotten.\n﴿أَلَمْ أَعْهَدْ إِلَيْكُمْ يَا بَنِي آدَمَ أَن لَّا تَعْبُدُوا الشَّيْطَانَ ۖ إِنَّهُ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِينٌ ٦٠ وَأَنِ اعْبُدُونِي ۚ هَـٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيمٌ ٦١﴾\nDid I not enjoin upon you, O children of Adam, that you not worship Satan - [for] indeed, he is to you a clear enemy - And that you worship [only] Me? This is a straight path.\n[Ya-Sin: 60, 61]\n2. Every prophet tried to stop his people from ‘polytheism’ or ‘shirk’:\n﴿لَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ فَقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ إِنِّي أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ٥٩﴾\nWe had certainly sent Noah to his people, and he said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a tremendous Day.\n[Al-A’raf: 59]\nHud(as) said:\n﴿وَإِلَىٰ عَادٍ أَخَاهُمْ هُودًا ۗ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۚ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ٦٥﴾\nAnd to the 'Aad [We sent] their brother Hud. He said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. Then will you not fear Him?\"\n[Al-A’raf: 65]\nThat is, why do you not fear Allah(swt) while ascribing partners to Him?\nSaleh(as) said:\nقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۖ قَدْ جَاءَتْكُم بَيِّنَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ ۖ\n\"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. There has come to you clear evidence from your Lord.”\n[Al-A’raf: 73]\nShuaib(as) said:\nقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۖ قَدْ جَاءَتْكُم بَيِّنَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ\n\"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. There has come to you clear evidence from your Lord.”\n[Al-A’raf: 85]\nAnd this was the essential message of all the prophets:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ بَعَثْنَا فِي كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ رَّسُولًا أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ وَاجْتَنِبُوا الطَّاغُوتَ ۖ فَمِنْهُم مَّنْ هَدَى اللَّـهُ وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ حَقَّتْ عَلَيْهِ الضَّلَالَةُ ۚ فَسِيرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ فَانظُرُوا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ ٣٦﴾\nAnd We certainly sent into every nation a messenger, [saying], \"Worship Allah and avoid Taghut.\" And among them were those whom Allah guided, and among them were those upon whom error was [deservedly] decreed. So proceed through the earth and observe how was the end of the deniers.\n[An-Nahl: 36]\nLuqman also stopped his son from shirk:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ لُقْمَانُ لِابْنِهِ وَهُوَ يَعِظُهُ يَا بُنَيَّ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِاللَّـهِ ۖ إِنَّ الشِّرْكَ لَظُلْمٌ عَظِيمٌ ١٣﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when Luqman said to his son while he was instructing him, \"O my son, do not associate [anything] with Allah. Indeed, association [with him] is great injustice.\"\n[Luqman: 13]\n3. Allah(swt) has made evident countless signs in His vast Creation which prove His Oneness. Anyone with understanding can discern them and arrive at the ultimate truth of ‘Tawheed’ or ‘monotheism’ and stay away from the most sinful act of associating partners with Allah(swt).\n﴿الَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْأَرْضَ فِرَاشًا وَالسَّمَاءَ بِنَاءً وَأَنزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً فَأَخْرَجَ بِهِ مِنَ الثَّمَرَاتِ رِزْقًا لَّكُمْ ۖ فَلَا تَجْعَلُوا لِلَّـهِ أَندَادًا وَأَنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ ٢٢﴾\n[He] who made for you the earth a bed [spread out] and the sky a ceiling and sent down from the sky, rain and brought forth thereby fruits as provision for you. So do not attribute to Allah equals while you know [that there is nothing similar to Him].\n[Al-Baqara: 22]\n4. Finally after sending the Last Prophet Muhammad(saws), Allah(swt) has shut all the doors of shirk. That is why the people committing shirk have no excuse to say they weren’t warned and the polytheists will say in fear:\n﴿ثُمَّ لَمْ تَكُن فِتْنَتُهُمْ إِلَّا أَن قَالُوا وَاللَّـهِ رَبِّنَا مَا كُنَّا مُشْرِكِينَ ٢٣﴾\nThen there will be no [excuse upon] examination except they will say, \"By Allah, our Lord, we were not those who associated.\"\n[Al-An’am: 23]\nBut they will be liars in their claim. That is why on the Day of Judgement their mouths will be sealed and their hands and legs will give evidence.\n﴿الْيَوْمَ نَخْتِمُ عَلَىٰ أَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَتُكَلِّمُنَا أَيْدِيهِمْ وَتَشْهَدُ أَرْجُلُهُم بِمَا كَانُوا يَكْسِبُونَ ٦٥﴾\nThat Day, We will seal over their mouths, and their hands will speak to Us, and their feet will testify about what they used to earn.\n[Ya-Sin: 65]\nAllah(swt) will never forgive the one who commits shirk:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَن يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَمَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّـهِ فَقَدِ افْتَرَىٰ إِثْمًا عَظِيمًا ٤٨﴾\nIndeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And he who associates others with Allah has certainly fabricated a tremendous sin.\n[An-Nisa: 48]\nAt another place it says:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَن يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَمَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّـهِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلَالًا بَعِيدًا ١١٦﴾\nIndeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And he who associates others with Allah has certainly gone far astray.\n[An-Nisa: 116]\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) was once asked, “What is the greatest sin in the sight of Allah(swt)?”\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “That you set up a rival unto Him when He(swt) Alone has created you.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 4477 and Sahih Muslim, 86)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“Shall I tell you what the major sins are?” The people replied, “Yes! O Apostle of Allah(swt)!” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Ascribing partners to Allah(swt), disobeying one’s parents and giving false testimony.” (Sahih Bukhari, 2654 and Sahih Muslim, 87)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Stay away from seven major sins.” The people asked,”What are they?” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “Ascribing partners to Allah(swt), practicing magic, killing someone unjustly, consuming interest, taking the wealth of the orphan, running away from fighting in the way of Allah(swt), and slandering the believing and chaste women.” (Sahih Bukhari, 2766 and Sahih Muslim, 89)\nWhen Verse-12 of Surah-60, Al-Mumtahina was revealed, among the things about which the Holy Prophet(saws) took pledge from the women was the oath that they would never associate anything with Allah(swt).\nAnd Zareer-bin-Abdullah narrates that the pledge which he took at the hand of the Holy Prophet(saws) was:\n“There is none worthy of worship other than Allah(swt) and Muhammad(saws) is His prophet.” (Sahih Bukhari, 2157 and Sahih Muslim, 56)\nHow did ‘shirk’ or ‘polytheism’ start:\nThe main reason why shirk started was the deception of the satan. When some prophet or a great and pious person dies, his followers are very sad and grief-stricken and they lose some of their sense of understanding. This is the right time for the satan to strike. He soothes the people saying he will help them overcome their grief. He encourages them to build a structure over the grave of the departed person which slowly becomes a place of worship. Over a period of time, people start prostrating in front of it, circumambulating it and even invoking the dead person to grant their wishes. So the person who has spent his entire life worshipping none other than Allah(swt) becomes the object of worship himself after his death. That is why the Holy Prophet(saws) has forbidden the building of structures over graves. (See: Sahih Muslim, 968)\nThe building of structures and tombs over graves, decorating them, making offerings to them, building mosques over them clearly goes against this command of the Holy Prophet(saws). These are nothing but the works of satan. Let us look at one other way in which the satan misleads men. When some prophet or pious person or rishi dies and his followers are immersed in grief, the satan encourages them to build an idol of the departed person so that by looking at it they can think about their preacher and soothe their troubled hearts. Slowly they start worshipping these man-made idols. Referring to this the Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ ضُرِبَ مَثَلٌ فَاسْتَمِعُوا لَهُ ۚ إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّـهِ لَن يَخْلُقُوا ذُبَابًا وَلَوِ اجْتَمَعُوا لَهُ ۖ وَإِن يَسْلُبْهُمُ الذُّبَابُ شَيْئًا لَّا يَسْتَنقِذُوهُ مِنْهُ ۚ ضَعُفَ الطَّالِبُ وَالْمَطْلُوبُ ٧٣﴾\nO people, an example is presented, so listen to it. Indeed, those you invoke besides Allah will never create [as much as] a fly, even if they gathered together for that purpose. And if the fly should steal away from them a [tiny] thing, they could not recover it from him. Weak are the pursuer and pursued.\n[Al-Hajj: 73]\nIn fact these are the plots of satan who keeps thinking up new ones to keep men away from the worship of Allah(swt)."],[299,"§Shuaib(as)\nAllah(swt) sent Shuaib(as) as a prophet to the people of Madyan. This tribe inhabited the place of Madyan which was named after Madyan, the son of Ibraheem(as) and Keturah. They lived on the eastern and western shores of the bay of Aqba. Shuaib(as) was from their fourth generation. That is why in the Holy Quran he is called ‘Aqa’ which means ‘brother’.\nوَإِلَىٰ مَدْيَنَ أَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا\nAnd to [the people of] Madyan [We sent] their brother Shu'ayb.\n[Al-A’raf: 85]\nوَإِلَىٰ مَدْيَنَ أَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا\nAnd to Madyan [We sent] their brother Shu'ayb.\n[Hud: 84]\nLike the other prophets, Shuaib(as) called his people to the worship of Allah(swt) as this was the basic message of all the prophets. They were committing all sorts of sins. They cheated in the measurement of things. They took more but gave less:\n﴿وَإِلَىٰ مَدْيَنَ أَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ۗ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّـهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَـٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۖ قَدْ جَاءَتْكُم بَيِّنَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ ۖ فَأَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَالْمِيزَانَ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ أَشْيَاءَهُمْ وَلَا تُفْسِدُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ بَعْدَ إِصْلَاحِهَا ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ٨٥﴾\nAnd to [the people of] Madyan [We sent] their brother Shu'ayb. He said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. There has come to you clear evidence from your Lord. So fulfill the measure and weight and do not deprive people of their due and cause not corruption upon the earth after its reformation. That is better for you, if you should be believers.\n[Al-A’raf: 85]\nCheating in the matter of measuring things creates mischief on earth because people start hating each other and this is not conducive for the existence of a peaceful society.\nقَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۖ وَلَا تَنقُصُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيزَانَ ۚ\nHe said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him. And do not decrease from the measure and the scale.\n[Hud: 84]\nBut the people of Madyan did not stop worshipping their false deities. On the other hand, they started warning and threatening Shuaib(as):\nقَالُوا يَا شُعَيْبُ أَصَلَاتُكَ تَأْمُرُكَ أَن نَّتْرُكَ مَا يَعْبُدُ آبَاؤُنَا أَوْ أَن نَّفْعَلَ فِي أَمْوَالِنَا مَا نَشَاءُ ۖ\nThey said, \"O Shu'ayb, does your prayer command you that we should leave what our fathers worship or not do with our wealth what we please?\n[Hud: 87]\nThe polytheists stubbornly follow the practices of their forefathers. However much it is explained to them that what they are doing is against the religion of Allah(swt) and the message of all the prophets, they remain firm in their disbelief and argue that they cannot leave what their ancestors have been doing for centuries. And they taunt the person asking him, if he is the only one having knowledge. The tribe of Shuaib(as) said:\nإِنَّكَ لَأَنتَ الْحَلِيمُ الرَّشِيدُ\n“Indeed, you are the forbearing, the discerning!\"\n[Hud: 87]\nThen they started threatening Shuaib(as):\nقَالَ الْمَلَأُ الَّذِينَ اسْتَكْبَرُوا مِن قَوْمِهِ لَنُخْرِجَنَّكَ يَا شُعَيْبُ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَكَ مِن قَرْيَتِنَا أَوْ لَتَعُودُنَّ فِي مِلَّتِنَا\nSaid the eminent ones who were arrogant among his people, \"We will surely evict you, O Shu'ayb, and those who have believed with you from our city, or you must return to our religion.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 88]\nAnd then they said to the people of the tribe:\n﴿وَقَالَ الْمَلَأُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِن قَوْمِهِ لَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتُمْ شُعَيْبًا إِنَّكُمْ إِذًا لَّخَاسِرُونَ ٩٠﴾\nSaid the eminent ones who disbelieved among his people, \"If you should follow Shu'ayb, indeed, you would then be losers.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 90]\nThe same thing happened to the people of the tribe of Madyan which had happened to the other disbelieving tribes; that is they incurred the wrath of Allah(swt):\n﴿فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَأَصْبَحُوا فِي دَارِهِمْ جَاثِمِينَ ٩١ الَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا شُعَيْبًا كَأَن لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيهَا ۚ الَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا شُعَيْبًا كَانُوا هُمُ الْخَاسِرِينَ ٩٢﴾\nSo the earthquake seized them, and they became within their home [corpses] fallen prone. Those who denied Shu'ayb - it was as though they had never resided there. Those who denied Shu'ayb - it was they who were the losers.\n[Al-A’raf: 91, 92]\n﴿وَلَمَّا جَاءَ أَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا شُعَيْبًا وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَأَخَذَتِ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَأَصْبَحُوا فِي دِيَارِهِمْ جَاثِمِينَ ٩٤﴾\nAnd when Our command came, We saved Shu'ayb and those who believed with him, by mercy from Us. And the shriek seized those who had wronged, and they became within their homes [corpses] fallen prone.\n[Hud: 94]\nThen Shuaib(as) went away towards Aika which was a forest on the shores of Kulzum and conveyed the message of Allah(swt) to the people there. Nothing can be said about this tribe but that they were not from the tribe of Shuaib(as). That is why Shuaib(as) is not addressed as brother. But even these people rejected the message of Shuaib(as):\n﴿كَذَّبَ أَصْحَابُ الْأَيْكَةِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٧٦ إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ شُعَيْبٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ١٧٧ إِنِّي لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ١٧٨﴾\nThe companions of the thicket denied the messengers. When Shu'ayb said to them, \"Will you not fear Allah? Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 176-178]\nThat is, you worship false gods and goddesses and holy persons when you have all been created by Allah(swt) and you very well know it. And you even cheat in the matter of measuring things:\n﴿أَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَلَا تَكُونُوا مِنَ الْمُخْسِرِينَ ١٨١ وَزِنُوا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيمِ ١٨٢ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ أَشْيَاءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِي الْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ ١٨٣﴾\nGive full measure and do not be of those who cause loss. And weigh with an even balance. And do not deprive people of their due and do not commit abuse on earth, spreading corruption.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 181-183]\nBut the people of Aika also did not pay heed to the message of Shuaib(as) and rejected him as a result of which Allah(swt) seized them in a terrible punishment:\n﴿فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَخَذَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمِ الظُّلَّةِ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ١٨٩﴾\nAnd they denied him, so the punishment of the day of the black cloud seized them. Indeed, it was the punishment of a terrible day.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 189]\nIn this way the Holy Quran describes many tribes who rejected the prophets who were sent for their guidance and were therefore punished by Allah(swt).\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was also a true prophet of Allah(swt) who was given the miraculous Holy Quran. If the people reject him and the book brought by him, then even they will have to face the wrath of Allah(swt). Nothing is mentioned either in the Holy Quran or the sahih hadith as to where Shuaib(as) went after the calamity of Aika. Many scholars are of the opinion that like the other prophets, Shuaib(as) went to Makkah where he passed away. But this view is not reliable. Some other scholars say that after the destruction of Aika, Shuaib(as) continued living in those forests worshipping Allah(swt) and died there itself and was buried in those forests.\nThere are varying opinions regarding the period during which Shuaib(as) lived. Some scholars are of the opinion that this is the same Shuaib, who met Musa(as) (See ‘Musa(as)’) and Musa(as) married one of his daughters. Some other scholars feel that the person who met Musa(as) was someone else who was in no way related to Shuaib(as). He was some pious person of Madyan and it says in the Taurah that his name was Jethro. This is the view of Ibn-Abbas and other scholars. Shuaib(as) lived before the time of Musa(as) and this can be deduced from the Holy Quran also. In Surah-A’raf, Musa(as) is described after Nuh, Hud, Saleh, Lut and Shuaib(as):\nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِن بَعْدِهِم مُّوسَىٰ بِآيَاتِنَا إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَئِهِ فَظَلَمُوا بِهَا ۖ\nThen We sent after them Moses with Our signs to Pharaoh and his establishment, but they were unjust toward them.\n[Al-A’raf: 103]\nIn the same way in Surah-Hud, Allah(swt) first describes Nuh(as) (See: Verse-25), then Hud(as) (See: Verse-50) and then Saleh(as) (See: Verse-61), then Ibraheem(as) (See: Verse-69), then Lut(as) (See: Verse-77) and then Shuaib(as) (See: Verse-84) and then Musa(as) (See: Verse-96). From this order we understand that Shuaib(as) lived before Musa(as). Shuaib(as) went away into the forests after the destruction of Aika and died there. Madyan was reestablished and Musa(as) went there after coming out of Egypt. (For detailed information see ‘Musa(as)’)."],[300,"§Shura(consultation)\n‘Shura’ means discussion or consultation. Islam is the first religion which orders consultation for running a state. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِرَبِّهِمْ وَأَقَامُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَأَمْرُهُمْ شُورَىٰ بَيْنَهُمْ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنَاهُمْ يُنفِقُونَ ٣٨﴾\nAnd those who have responded to their lord and established prayer and whose affair is [determined by] consultation among themselves, and from what We have provided them, they spend.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 38]\nAllah(swt) commanded the Holy Prophet(saws):\nفَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ وَشَاوِرْهُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ\nSo pardon them and ask forgiveness for them and consult them in the matter.\n[Al-i-Imran: 159]\nBut this is applicable only to worldly matters. In case of the commands of Allah(swt) or the Holy Prophet(saws), there is no question of consultation or discussion; it is obligatory to follow the commands of Allah(swt) and the Holy Prophet(saws). As to the command for consultations in the worldly matters, no specific rules have been laid down; the people can go about them as they wish. One way to do this is by the appointment of an advisory committee by the ruler. This council can have scholars and specialists from all fields and they can advise the ruler on various matters if he seeks their opinion. The rights and duties of this council can be decided by the ruler. But it is not binding on the ruler to follow the recommendations of this council because the range of knowledge which the ruler has about the kingdom and the people is comprehensive compared to the specific knowledge of the members of the council. He has the internal knowledge about problems and the state secrets. He is the best judge of the effect of various decisions on the state and the people. He can take a decision based on the view-point of the council. The Holy Prophet(saws) was given the command to take decisions after consultations in all worldly matters. But it was not compulsory for him to do so. After consulting the people, he(saws) would take the final decision based on what he(saws) thought was best because the wisdom and perspective which Allah(swt) had granted to the Holy Prophet(saws) was not granted to anyone else."],[301,"§Sinai\n‘Sinai’ is the desert which lies between the gulf of Aqba and the gulf of Suez. Its length is approximately three hundred kilometers and the breadth is approximately one hundred and fifty kilometers. Bani-Israel wandered in this desert for forty years. ‘Sinai’ is also the name of a mountain which is called ‘Tur’. It was on this mountain that Musa(as) was given the Taurah. At two places in the Holy Quran, ‘Sinai’ has been used with ‘Tur’:\nوَشَجَرَةً تَخْرُجُ مِن طُورِ سَيْنَاءَ\nAnd [We brought forth] a tree issuing from Mount Sinai.\n[Al-Mu’minun: 20]\n﴿وَالتِّينِ وَالزَّيْتُونِ ١ وَطُورِ سِينِينَ ٢﴾\nBy the fig and the olive. And [by] Mount Sinai.\n[At-Teen: 1, 2]\nMount Sinai is also called Mount Horeb and is described many times in the Taurah. Bani-Israel had camped here and various events took place."],[302,"§Sky\nThe sky which we can see always is a living proof of the Majesty of Allah(swt). But very few people derive any lesson from this vast spread out creation. The sky is described in various ways in the Holy Quran and none other than Allah(swt) could have created this limitless roof over our heads which does not require any support.\nخَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ بِغَيْرِ عَمَدٍ تَرَوْنَهَا\nHe created the heavens without pillars that you see\n[Luqman: 10]\nThe sky is not one but seven in number:\n﴿الَّذِي خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمَاوَاتٍ طِبَاقًا ۖ مَّا تَرَىٰ فِي خَلْقِ الرَّحْمَـٰنِ مِن تَفَاوُتٍ ۖ فَارْجِعِ الْبَصَرَ هَلْ تَرَىٰ مِن فُطُورٍ ٣﴾\n[And] who created seven heavens in layers. You do not see in the creation of the Most Merciful any inconsistency. So return [your] vision [to the sky]; do you see any breaks?\n[Al-Mulk: 3]\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَوْا كَيْفَ خَلَقَ اللَّـهُ سَبْعَ سَمَاوَاتٍ طِبَاقًا ١٥﴾\nDo you not consider how Allah has created seven heavens in layers.\n[Nuh: 15]\nProclaiming His might Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran that on the Day of Judgement these vast skies will be in his grip.\n﴿وَمَا قَدَرُوا اللَّـهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهِ وَالْأَرْضُ جَمِيعًا قَبْضَتُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَالسَّمَاوَاتُ مَطْوِيَّاتٌ بِيَمِينِهِ ۚ سُبْحَانَهُ وَتَعَالَىٰ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ ٦٧﴾\nThey have not appraised Allah with true appraisal, while the earth entirely will be [within] His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand. Exalted is He and high above what they associate with Him.\n[Az-Zumar: 67]\nOn the night of Meraj, Allah(swt) took the Holy Prophet(saws) on a tour of the seven skies. The description of Meraj is given in Surah ‘Isra’.\nExamples (analogies) of sky in the Holy Quran:\nThe disbelievers being compared to someone climbing up to the sky:\n﴿فَمَن يُرِدِ اللَّـهُ أَن يَهْدِيَهُ يَشْرَحْ صَدْرَهُ لِلْإِسْلَامِ ۖ وَمَن يُرِدْ أَن يُضِلَّهُ يَجْعَلْ صَدْرَهُ ضَيِّقًا حَرَجًا كَأَنَّمَا يَصَّعَّدُ فِي السَّمَاءِ ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يَجْعَلُ اللَّـهُ الرِّجْسَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ ١٢٥﴾\nSo whoever Allah wants to guide - He expands his breast to [contain] Islam; and whoever He wants to misguide - He makes his breast tight and constricted as though he were climbing into the sky. Thus does Allah place defilement upon those who do not believe.\n[Al-An’am: 125]\nA good word being compared to a tree whose branches have reached the sky:\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ ضَرَبَ اللَّـهُ مَثَلًا كَلِمَةً طَيِّبَةً كَشَجَرَةٍ طَيِّبَةٍ أَصْلُهَا ثَابِتٌ وَفَرْعُهَا فِي السَّمَاءِ ٢٤﴾\nHave you not considered how Allah presents an example, [making] a good word like a good tree, whose root is firmly fixed and its branches [high] in the sky?\n[Ibraheem: 24]\nComparison of a polytheist(mushrik) to somebody who has fallen from the sky:\nوَمَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَكَأَنَّمَا خَرَّ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ فَتَخْطَفُهُ الطَّيْرُ أَوْ تَهْوِي بِهِ الرِّيحُ فِي مَكَانٍ سَحِيقٍ\nAnd he who associates with Allah - it is as though he had fallen from the sky and was snatched by the birds or the wind carried him down into a remote place.\n[Al-Hajj: 31]\nThe seven skies exalt Allah(swt) by His praise:\n﴿تُسَبِّحُ لَهُ السَّمَاوَاتُ السَّبْعُ وَالْأَرْضُ وَمَن فِيهِنَّ ۚ وَإِن مِّن شَيْءٍ إِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهِ وَلَـٰكِن لَّا تَفْقَهُونَ تَسْبِيحَهُمْ ۗ إِنَّهُ كَانَ حَلِيمًا غَفُورًا ٤٤﴾\nThe seven heavens and the earth and whatever is in them exalt Him. And there is not a thing except that it exalts [Allah] by His praise, but you do not understand their [way of] exalting. Indeed, He is ever Forbearing and Forgiving.\n[Bani-Israel: 44]\nAll the creatures of the skies prostrate before Allah(swt):\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّ اللَّـهَ يَسْجُدُ لَهُ مَن فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَن فِي الْأَرْضِ وَالشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ وَالنُّجُومُ وَالْجِبَالُ وَالشَّجَرُ وَالدَّوَابُّ وَكَثِيرٌ مِّنَ النَّاسِ ۖ وَكَثِيرٌ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِ الْعَذَابُ ۗ وَمَن يُهِنِ اللَّـهُ فَمَا لَهُ مِن مُّكْرِمٍ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يَشَاءُ ۩ ١٨﴾\nDo you not see that to Allah prostrates whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth and the sun, the moon, the stars, the mountains, the trees, the moving creatures and many of the people? But upon many the punishment has been justified. And he whom Allah humiliates - for him there is no bestower of honor. Indeed, Allah does what He wills.\n[Al-Hajj: 18]\n﴿إِنَّ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ لَآيَاتٍ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ٣﴾\nIndeed, within the heavens and earth are signs for the believers.\n[Al-Jathiya: 3]"],[303,"§Snake\n‘Snake’ is a creature which crawls. It is mentioned in the story of Musa(as) in the Holy Quran. When Allah(swt) decided to show a miracle to Musa(as) He(swt) said:\n﴿وَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ ١٧ قَالَ هِيَ عَصَايَ أَتَوَكَّأُ عَلَيْهَا وَأَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلَىٰ غَنَمِي وَلِيَ فِيهَا مَآرِبُ أُخْرَىٰ ١٨﴾\nAnd what is that in your right hand, O Moses?\" He said, \"It is my staff; I lean upon it, and I bring down leaves for my sheep and I have therein other uses.\"\n[Ta-Ha: 17, 18]\nAllah(swt) knew that Musa(as) had a staff in his hand; but He(swt) wanted to show him a miracle so He(swt) commanded:\n﴿قَالَ أَلْقِهَا يَا مُوسَىٰ ١٩ فَأَلْقَاهَا فَإِذَا هِيَ حَيَّةٌ تَسْعَىٰ ٢٠ قَالَ خُذْهَا وَلَا تَخَفْ ۖ سَنُعِيدُهَا سِيرَتَهَا الْأُولَىٰ ٢١﴾\n[Allah] said, \"Throw it down, O Moses.\" So he threw it down, and thereupon it was a snake, moving swiftly. [Allah] said, \"Seize it and fear not; We will return it to its former condition.\n[Ta-Ha: 19-21] [Al-A’raf: 107]\nAnd then when there was a competition between Musa(as) and the magicians before the Pharaoh(Firaun), the magicians threw down their ropes and staffs and said:\n﴿قَالُوا بِعِزَّةِ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْغَالِبُونَ ٤٤ فَأَلْقَىٰ مُوسَىٰ عَصَاهُ فَإِذَا هِيَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَأْفِكُونَ ٤٥ فَأُلْقِيَ السَّحَرَةُ سَاجِدِينَ ٤٦ قَالُوا آمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ٤٧ رَبِّ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ ٤٨﴾\n\"By the might of Pharaoh, indeed it is we who are predominant.\" Then Moses threw his staff, and at once it devoured what they falsified. So the magicians fell down in prostration [to Allah]. They said, \"We have believed in the Lord of the worlds, The Lord of Moses and Aaron.\"\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 44-48]"],[304,"§Soor\n‘Soor’ means a ‘horn’ or a ‘trumpet’. Soor is described at ten places in the Holy Quran and at every place it has the same meaning. The ‘Soor’ will be blown on Doomsday and its sound will be so terrifying that all the people will fall unconscious. Then, it will be blown a second time and the people will be resurrected and will assemble in the grounds of ‘Hashr’ to give an account of their deeds.\nوَلَهُ الْمُلْكُ يَوْمَ يُنفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ\nAnd His is the dominion [on] the Day the Horn is blown.\n[Al-An’am: 73]\nوَنُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ فَجَمَعْنَاهُمْ جَمْعًا\nThe Horn will be blown, and We will assemble them in [one] assembly.\n[Al-Kahf: 99]\n﴿يَوْمَ يُنفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ ۚ وَنَحْشُرُ الْمُجْرِمِينَ يَوْمَئِذٍ زُرْقًا ١٠٢﴾\nThe Day the Horn will be blown. And We will gather the criminals, that Day, blue-eyed.\n[Ta-Ha: 102]\n﴿فَإِذَا نُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ فَلَا أَنسَابَ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَلَا يَتَسَاءَلُونَ ١٠١﴾\nSo when the Horn is blown, no relationship will there be among them that Day, nor will they ask about one another.\n[Al-Mu’minun: 101]\n﴿وَيَوْمَ يُنفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ فَفَزِعَ مَن فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَن فِي الْأَرْضِ إِلَّا مَن شَاءَ اللَّـهُ ۚ وَكُلٌّ أَتَوْهُ دَاخِرِينَ ٨٧﴾\nAnd [warn of] the Day the Horn will be blown, and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will be terrified except whom Allah wills. And all will come to Him humbled.\n[An-Naml: 87]\n﴿وَنُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ فَإِذَا هُم مِّنَ الْأَجْدَاثِ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ يَنسِلُونَ ٥١﴾\nAnd the Horn will be blown; and at once from the graves to their Lord they will hasten.\n[Ya-Sin: 51]\n﴿وَنُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ فَصَعِقَ مَن فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَن فِي الْأَرْضِ إِلَّا مَن شَاءَ اللَّـهُ ۖ ثُمَّ نُفِخَ فِيهِ أُخْرَىٰ فَإِذَا هُمْ قِيَامٌ يَنظُرُونَ ٦٨﴾\nAnd the Horn will be blown, and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will fall dead except whom Allah wills. Then it will be blown again, and at once they will be standing, looking on.\n[Az-Zumar: 68]\n﴿وَنُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ يَوْمُ الْوَعِيدِ ٢٠﴾\nAnd the Horn will be blown. That is the Day of [carrying out] the threat.\n[Qaf: 20]\n﴿فَإِذَا نُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ نَفْخَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ ١٣ وَحُمِلَتِ الْأَرْضُ وَالْجِبَالُ فَدُكَّتَا دَكَّةً وَاحِدَةً ١٤ فَيَوْمَئِذٍ وَقَعَتِ الْوَاقِعَةُ ١٥﴾\nThen when the Horn is blown with one blast. And the earth and the mountains are lifted and leveled with one blow - Then on that Day, the Resurrection will occur.\n[Al-Haqqa: 13-15]\n﴿يَوْمَ يُنفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ فَتَأْتُونَ أَفْوَاجًا ١٨﴾\nThe Day the Horn is blown and you will come forth in multitudes.\n[An-Naba: 18]\nFrom the above verses it is clear that the trumpet will be blown twice. This is understood from the above verse of Surah-Az-Zumar. The same fact is also narrated in a hadith of Sahih Muslim. (See: Sahih Muslim:2940)\nSome scholars are of the opinion that the trumpet will be blown thrice. When it is blown the first time, all that is on the earth and the skies will be terrified as described in Verse-87 of Surah-An-Naml. When it is blown a second time, everyone will become unconscious. And when it is blown a third time, everyone will be resurrected from their graves as described in Verse-68 of Surah-Az-Zumar. But in our opinion the trumpet will be blown only twice. Everyone being terrified as described in Surah-An-Naml and everyone becoming unconscious as described in Surah-Az-Zumar mean the same thing. Allah(swt) will protect some from the terror as mentioned in Surah-An-Naml and in the same sense, He(swt) will save them from becoming unconscious. It is corroborated in a sahih hadith in which the Holy Prophet(saws) says:\n\"Do not give me superiority over other prophets, for on the Day of Resurrection when the trumpet is blown all the people will fall unconscious except those whom Allah(swt) wills and when it is blown a second time I will be the first to emerge from the earth, and will see Musa (Moses) standing and holding one of the legs of the Throne. I will not know whether Musa (Moses) has fallen unconscious and got up before me or the first unconsciousness on Mount Tur was sufficient for him.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3414 and Sahih Muslim, 2373)\nIn fact, from this hadith we understand that the terror described in Surah-An-Naml is the same as becoming unconscious as in the same verse it says –‘except Whom Allah wills’, that is some will not become unconscious.\nIt is important to make it clear that it is not established that the angel Israfeel will blow the trumpet. The hadith mentioning this is ‘Zaeef’."],[305,"§Spider\nSpider is called ‘Ankaboot’ in Arabic. There is a surah by this name in the Holy Quran which has a total of 69 verses and was revealed in Makkah.\nIn olden days, a weak thing was compared to a spider’s web which could break with just one gust of wind. In the same way, the life of man is like the web of a spider which can end any moment. But in the Holy Quran, the web of a spider is compared to ‘shirk’ or ‘polytheism’:\n﴿مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ اتَّخَذُوا مِن دُونِ اللَّـهِ أَوْلِيَاءَ كَمَثَلِ الْعَنكَبُوتِ اتَّخَذَتْ بَيْتًا ۖ وَإِنَّ أَوْهَنَ الْبُيُوتِ لَبَيْتُ الْعَنكَبُوتِ ۖ لَوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ ٤١﴾\nThe example of those who take allies other than Allah is like that of the spider who takes a home. And indeed, the weakest of homes is the home of the spider, if they only knew.\n[Al-Ankaboot: 41]\nWorshipping and supplicating and invoking someone other than Allah(swt) is like taking shelter in the house of a spider. This verse is very comprehensive and has many deep and hidden meanings. That is why after reading this verse countless people have become ‘monotheists’ and started believing in the Oneness of Allah(swt) and have taken shelter in the cool shade of Islam."],[306,"§Stealing\nStealing is a social evil. When a society is afflicted with this disease, it becomes difficult to control it. Among the rights of an individual which Islam protects, one is the safety of his wealth. That is the reason stealing has been declared a major sin. The Holy Prophet(saws) while asking a person taking ‘Ba’ith’ that he should not declare anyone other than Allah(swt) as witness, also makes him swear that he will not steal. It is the duty of the ruler to rid the society of this evil.\nTo keep the society free from this evil, Islam lays down a few rules. One is that the ruler should govern his kingdom in such a way that no one goes hungry and the basic needs of everybody are fulfilled through proper livelihood. The people who are incapable of earning their livelihood should be given a monthly pension from the royal treasury. Then the evil consequences of stealing should be explained to the people. If after all this the people persist in stealing then the punishment ordained in Islam should be given to them.\nIn this way the society will be rid of this evil.\nPunishment for stealing:\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَالسَّارِقُ وَالسَّارِقَةُ فَاقْطَعُوا أَيْدِيَهُمَا جَزَاءً بِمَا كَسَبَا نَكَالًا مِّنَ اللَّـهِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ ٣٨﴾\n[As for] the thief, the male and the female, amputate their hands in recompense for what they committed as a deterrent [punishment] from Allah. And Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 38]\nAllah(swt) in His(swt) infinite wisdom knows best why He(swt) has decided this punishment. The cutting off of one hand can ensure the safety of the whole society as it acts as a deterrent to others. It is a must to keep in mind the following points while giving the punishment:\n1. The property should have been stolen from some secure place. If it has been taken from some unsecured or open place, then the punishment does not apply.\n2. There is no doubt about the property being stolen. If there is any doubt then the punishment does not apply. For example if a servant has stolen from his master, if a son has stolen from his father or if a wife has stolen from her husband; that is someone has taken something in which he has a share then the punishment does not apply. If the court wishes then it can give him Taazir or ‘a light punishment’.\n3. The crime should be proved in a court of law and the sentence should also be given there; else the punishment cannot be implemented.\nThere are a few other conditions which have to be fulfilled before implementing this punishment.\nIt is important to mention here that while ridding the society of its evils, Islam does not make any distinction between people. This is corroborated from the following sahih hadith. A woman was indicted for stealing. The people of Quraish asked Osama-bin-Zaid who was a favourite of the Holy Prophet(swt) to plead with him(saws) to let her off. The Holy Prophet(saws) told him, “You are making a distinction in the punishment ordained by Allah(swt).” He(saws) then summoned all the people and gave this sermon:\n“O People! The people who had come before you were destroyed because when a high-standing person committed robbery, he was let off while if a person from a lower sect stole something, he was punished. I swear in the name of Allah(swt) that even if my daughter Fatima steals something I will cut off her hand.” (Bukhari, 347 and Muslim, 1688)"],[307,"§Struggle(Strife)\nStrife is called ‘Muharba’ in Arabic. Muharba means to cause dissent and conflict in a country with the help of bands or groups and loot the people, kill them, burn their houses etc. These people are called ‘Muharib’. Referring to these people the Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِنَّمَا جَزَاءُ الَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَسَادًا أَن يُقَتَّلُوا أَوْ يُصَلَّبُوا أَوْ تُقَطَّعَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَأَرْجُلُهُم مِّنْ خِلَافٍ أَوْ يُنفَوْا مِنَ الْأَرْضِ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ لَهُمْ خِزْيٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا ۖ وَلَهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ ٣٣﴾\nIndeed, the penalty for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive upon earth [to cause] corruption is none but that they be killed or crucified or that their hands and feet be cut off from opposite sides or that they be exiled from the land. That is for them a disgrace in this world; and for them in the Hereafter is a great punishment.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 33]\nThe severe punishment is a lesson and deterrent to others because during the time of the Holy Prophet(saws), one such incident occurred upon which this verse was revealed and as a result such incidents were never again repeated.\nThe incident which occurred is described here. A few people from the tribes of Uqal and Uraina became Muslims and came to Madina. But the climate of Madina did not suit them and they fell ill. The Holy Prophet(saws) asked them to go to the outskirts of Madina where the zakat camels were kept and drink their urine and milk as medicine. They followed his advice and as a result regained their health. Then, they killed the shepherd and ran away with the camels. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know of this he(saws) sent some men after them to capture them. When they were brought back to Madina, their hands and feet were cut off, and their eyes were pierced with hot iron rods and they were thrown in the hot sun till they died. (Sahih Bukhari, 233 and Sahih Muslim, 1671)\nAfter this nobody dared to commit such an act. That is, this sort of punishment saved many lives. But if before being captured, the culprits surrender themselves, then they can be forgiven. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِلَّا الَّذِينَ تَابُوا مِن قَبْلِ أَن تَقْدِرُوا عَلَيْهِمْ ۖ فَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّـهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ٣٤﴾\nExcept for those who return [repenting] before you apprehend them. And know that Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 34]\nThis forgiveness is limited to the punishment of the state. But as far as the individual loss is concerned, be it murder or looting, the culprit will not be forgiven till the victim forgives him because the state does not have the right to infringe on the rights of the individuals."],[308,"§Suckling\nSee ‘Riza’at’"],[309,"§Sulaiman(as)\nSulaiman(as) was one of the great prophets of Bani-Israel. As his father Dawood(as) had other sons and Sulaiman(as) could not be the sole inheritor of his father’s wealth, he was made an inheritor of Dawood(as)’s prophethood and kingship. (See: Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-16)\nSulaiman(as) was born around 1045-1020 B.C. Maybe his father Dawood(as) perceived some special qualities in his son due to which he kept Sulaiman(as) with him while handling the matters of the kingdom. We come to know of this from the following verse of the Holy Quran:\nوَدَاوُودَ وَسُلَيْمَانَ إِذْ يَحْكُمَانِ فِي الْحَرْثِ إِذْ نَفَشَتْ فِيهِ غَنَمُ الْقَوْمِ\nAnd [mention] David and Solomon, when they judged concerning the field - when the sheep of a people overran it [at night].\n[Al-Anbiya: 78]\nIt is mentioned in the Bible that his father Dawood(as) was very fond of Sulaiman(as) as his mother Bathsheba was the favourite wife of Dawood(as) and he had promised her that Sulaiman(as) would be made the heir to his kingdom. But when Adoniah, the eldest son of Dawood(as) was making efforts to sit on the throne, Bathsheba reminded her husband of his promise. As a result there was a war between Sulaiman(as) and Adoniah in which Adoniah was killed. And in this way Dawood(as) declared his favourite son Sulaiman(as) his heir. (See: Bible, 1 Kings 1:10 and after that)\nWhatever the reasons, Dawood(as) made Sulaiman(as) his heir. According to the Bible, the first thing which Sulaiman(as) did after being made the king was to marry the daughter of the Egyptian Pharaoh. (See: Bible, 1 Kings, 3)\nIn this way he established friendly relations with the most powerful neighbor and ruled successfully for forty years and during his reign the Bani-Israel lived peacefully.\nExcellent qualities of Sulaiman(as):\n1. Allah(swt) had made the wind subservient to him. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلِسُلَيْمَانَ الرِّيحَ عَاصِفَةً تَجْرِي بِأَمْرِهِ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ الَّتِي بَارَكْنَا فِيهَا ۚ وَكُنَّا بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَالِمِينَ\nAnd to Solomon [We subjected] the wind, blowing forcefully, proceeding by his command toward the land which We had blessed. And We are ever, of all things, Knowing.\n[Al-Anbiya: 81]\nAt another place it says:\nوَلِسُلَيْمَانَ الرِّيحَ غُدُوُّهَا شَهْرٌ وَرَوَاحُهَا شَهْرٌ\nAnd to Solomon [We subjected] the wind - its morning [journey was that of] a month - and its afternoon [journey was that of] a month.\n[Saba: 12]\nAt another place it says:\nفَسَخَّرْنَا لَهُ الرِّيحَ تَجْرِي بِأَمْرِهِ رُخَاءً حَيْثُ أَصَابَ\nSo We subjected to him the wind blowing by his command, gently, wherever he directed.\n[Sad: 36]\nIt is not described either in the Holy Quran or in the sahih hadith as to how Sulaiman(as) went wherever he wished with the help of wind. Some of the commentators of the Holy Quran have said that he had a wooden throne with him. Sulaiman(as) would mount it along with a few essential things and the wind would carry him wherever he wished to go. In this way he could in one morning travel a distance which would normally take one month and in the same way he could travel a distance covered generally in one month in one afternoon. It is also mentioned in Surah-Al-Anbiya that Sulaiman(as) travelled this way to a land which was blessed by Allah(swt). From this we can deduce that his travels were till Palestine and the neighbouring places as those were the places in his kingdom.\nSome other scholars are of the opinion that Sulaiman(as) had many ships with him which he used in wars and also for trade purposes. In those days ships were totally dependent on the winds and as Allah(swt) had given Sulaiman(as) control over winds, he could make them take his ships wherever he pleased. When he wanted to go somewhere very fast, then he would order them to blow with full force and in case he wanted to just enjoy a ride or in the case of trade-ships, he would order the winds to blow mildly. In the Holy Quran the word ‘Aseefa’ is used for powerful winds and ‘rukha’ for gently blowing winds. The Bible also corroborates this. According to it, the ships roamed the Mediterranean sea (See: Bible, 1 Kings, Chapter 10). Even if the winds were not favourable Sulaiman(as) had no problem as he could control them. But coming back to the one month distance journeys which he covered in one morning and one afternoon, the areas within his kingdom could be reached in less than a month by sea. So where did he travel? Some scholars say that Sulaiman(as) travelled to other kingdoms also and the distance was such that it would normally take one month. Like the Tarsheesh which is mentioned in the Bible. Where is this Tarsheesh which took three years to reach as is mentioned in the Bible? (See: 1 Kings, 10:22). Some people say that it is a city near Gibraltar. (See Khamoos Muqaddas p.217). But this is just the author’s view. It seems that a mistake has been made in saying that ships travelled for years and thus Tarsheesh is near Spain. But in fact this Tarsheesh is the same as Tartush on the Mediterranean coast. And it takes one month to travel from Yafa ghat to Tartush as is mentioned in the Holy Quran.\n2. Allah(swt) taught Sulaiman(as) the language of the birds:\n﴿وَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمَانُ دَاوُودَ ۖ وَقَالَ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ عُلِّمْنَا مَنطِقَ الطَّيْرِ وَأُوتِينَا مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ ۖ إِنَّ هَـٰذَا لَهُوَ الْفَضْلُ الْمُبِينُ ١٦﴾\nAnd Solomon inherited David. He said, \"O people, we have been taught the language of birds, and we have been given from all things. Indeed, this is evident bounty.\"\n[An-Naml: 16]\nSulaiman(as) had a Hudhud bird with him. One day while all the birds were assembled, he found the Hudhud missing and asked:\n﴿وَتَفَقَّدَ الطَّيْرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِيَ لَا أَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ أَمْ كَانَ مِنَ الْغَائِبِينَ ٢٠﴾\nAnd he took attendance of the birds and said, \"Why do I not see the hoopoe - or is he among the absent?”\n[An-Naml: 20]\nFrom this we understand that Sulaiman(as) took attendance of the birds every day.\n3. Sulaiman(as) understood the language of the animals also as mentioned in the Holy Quran:\n﴿حَتَّىٰ إِذَا أَتَوْا عَلَىٰ وَادِ النَّمْلِ قَالَتْ نَمْلَةٌ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّمْلُ ادْخُلُوا مَسَاكِنَكُمْ لَا يَحْطِمَنَّكُمْ سُلَيْمَانُ وَجُنُودُهُ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ١٨﴾\nUntil, when they came upon the valley of the ants, an ant said, \"O ants, enter your dwellings that you not be crushed by Solomon and his soldiers while they perceive not.\"\n[An-Naml: 18]\n4. Both men and jinn were subservient to Sulaiman(as):\n﴿وَحُشِرَ لِسُلَيْمَانَ جُنُودُهُ مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنسِ وَالطَّيْرِ فَهُمْ يُوزَعُونَ ١٧﴾\nAnd gathered for Solomon were his soldiers of the jinn and men and birds, and they were [marching] in rows.\n[An-Naml: 17]\nHe allocated various tasks to the jinn:\n﴿وَأَسَلْنَا لَهُ عَيْنَ الْقِطْرِ ۖ وَمِنَ الْجِنِّ مَن يَعْمَلُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ بِإِذْنِ رَبِّهِ ۖ وَمَن يَزِغْ مِنْهُمْ عَنْ أَمْرِنَا نُذِقْهُ مِنْ عَذَابِ السَّعِيرِ ١٢ يَعْمَلُونَ لَهُ مَا يَشَاءُ مِن مَّحَارِيبَ وَتَمَاثِيلَ وَجِفَانٍ كَالْجَوَابِ وَقُدُورٍ رَّاسِيَاتٍ ۚ﴾\nAnd We made flow for him a spring of [liquid] copper. And among the jinn were those who worked for him by the permission of his Lord. And whoever deviated among them from Our command - We will make him taste of the punishment of the Blaze. They made for him what he willed of elevated chambers, statues, bowls like reservoirs, and stationary kettles.\n[Saba: 12-13]\nAs far as the making of statues is concerned, maybe it was allowed in the religion of those times. But with the advent of Islam, the making of statues has been forbidden as it may lead to shirk and polytheism.\nSulaiman(as) built huge palaces with the help of these jinn.\nIt is possible that Masjid-e-Aqsa was also built by jinn. One powerful jinn also says that before Sulaiman(as) can get up he can bring the throne of the Queen of Sheba to him. (See: Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-39)\nAnother jinn who was maybe not as powerful as the first one but who had knowledge of the ancient books of Allah(swt) said that he could bring the throne in the twinkling of an eye. (See: Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-40)\nWhen Sulaiman(as) saw the throne in front of him, he exclaimed:\nهَٰذَا مِن فَضْلِ رَبِّي لِيَبْلُوَنِي أَأَشْكُرُ أَمْ أَكْفُرُ ۖ وَمَن شَكَرَ فَإِنَّمَا يَشْكُرُ لِنَفْسِهِ ۖ وَمَن كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ رَبِّي غَنِيٌّ كَرِيمٌ\n\"This is from the favor of my Lord to test me whether I will be grateful or ungrateful. And whoever is grateful - his gratitude is only for [the benefit of] himself. And whoever is ungrateful - then indeed, my Lord is Free of need and Generous.\"\n[An-Naml: 40]\n5. Even the satan was under his control:\n﴿وَالشَّيَاطِينَ كُلَّ بَنَّاءٍ وَغَوَّاصٍ ٣٧ وَآخَرِينَ مُقَرَّنِينَ فِي الْأَصْفَادِ ٣٨﴾\nAnd [also] the devils [of jinn] - every builder and diver. And others bound together in shackles.\n[Sad: 37, 38]\nThat is, some jinn who worked for him built huge palaces for him while some others dived into the deep seas and brought forth precious stones and pearls. As for the ones who did not obey him, they were bound together in shackles. In this way Allah(swt) had granted a splendid kingdom to Sulaiman(as) and such a magnificent kingdom was neither granted to anyone before him nor to anyone after him. Sulaiman(as) had prayed to Allah(swt) for such a kingdom and Allah(swt) in His infinite mercy had granted it to him. (See: Quran, Surah-38, Sad, Verse-35)\nSatans are of the same kind as jinn. But whereas among the jinn, both Muslims and disbelievers are present, all the satans are enemies of Islam who disobey Allah(swt). It is narrated in a sahih hadith that one day when the Holy Prophet(saws) was offering salah, a satan was trying to spoil it but Allah(swt) helped the Holy Prophet(saws) overcome the satan. The Holy Prophet(saws) wanted to tie the satan to a pillar, but he(saws) remembered the invocation of Sulaiman(as):\n﴿قَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي وَهَبْ لِي مُلْكًا لَّا يَنبَغِي لِأَحَدٍ مِّن بَعْدِي ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْوَهَّابُ ٣٥﴾\nHe said, \"My Lord, forgive me and grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me. Indeed, You are the Bestower.\"\n[Sad: 35]\nAnd then the Holy Prophet(saws) let the satan go.\n(See Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, 1:102)\nAfter ruling for forty years, around 975 B.C, Sulaiman(as) passed away. Before his death, he completed the Masjid-e-Aqsa which his great grandfather Yaqub(as) had made for the worship of Allah(swt) but which had fallen into ruins as the Bani-Israel were engaged in various wars before Sulaiman(as). Dawood(as) again bought the place and rebuilt a part of it. But the entire work was completed during the reign of Sulaiman(as). That is why it is not correct to say that Sulaiman(as) built Masjid-e-Aqsa; Sulaiman(as) rebuilt it. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that there is a difference of forty years between the building of Masjid-e-Haram and Masjid-e-Aqsa. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 3115 and Sahih Muslim, 808) and as everybody knows Masjid-e-Haram was built by Ibraheem(as) who lived about one thousand years before Sulaiman(as). So, the correct version is Yaqub(as) built Masjid-e-Aqsa for the worship of Allah(swt) and Sulaiman(as) rebuilt it.\nSulaiman(as) was a great prophet sent for the guidance of the Jews. A prophet does not commit any major sins; he may make some small mistakes. From the Bible we get the impression that he was just a king whose empire was from the Euphrates to the Nile. While in many matters, his qualities have been exaggerated, in some other cases things have been written about him which go against the greatness of a prophet and it is pointless discussing them. (See: Bible, 1 Kings, 11:1-8)\nIt is the Holy Quran which mentions Sulaiman(as) as a great prophet and describes the special qualities and favours which Allah(swt) had bestowed upon him. But this does not mean that a prophet does not commit even small mistakes. But the difference is that he repents and seeks the forgiveness of Allah(swt) as it says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِذْ عُرِضَ عَلَيْهِ بِالْعَشِيِّ الصَّافِنَاتُ الْجِيَادُ ٣١ فَقَالَ إِنِّي أَحْبَبْتُ حُبَّ الْخَيْرِ عَن ذِكْرِ رَبِّي حَتَّىٰ تَوَارَتْ بِالْحِجَابِ ٣٢ رُدُّوهَا عَلَيَّ ۖ فَطَفِقَ مَسْحًا بِالسُّوقِ وَالْأَعْنَاقِ ٣٣﴾\n[Mention] when there were exhibited before him in the afternoon the poised [standing] racehorses. And he said, \"Indeed, I gave preference to the love of good [things] over the remembrance of my Lord until the sun disappeared into the curtain [of darkness].\" [He said], \"Return them to me,\" and set about striking [their] legs and necks.\n[Sad: 31-33]\nThat is, seeing the magnificent horses, Sulaiman(as) neglected to worship Allah(swt) till the sun set. That is why as a means of repentance, he killed the horses because it was due to the love of the horses that he could not worship Allah(swt). That is why we should discard every such thing which is a hindrance in the worship of Allah(swt). This seems to be the correct meaning. Some scholars have explained the verses in another way which does not seem to be correct. One other mistake which Sulaiman(as) did is described in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا سُلَيْمَانَ وَأَلْقَيْنَا عَلَىٰ كُرْسِيِّهِ جَسَدًا ثُمَّ أَنَابَ ٣٤﴾\nAnd We certainly tried Solomon and placed on his throne a body; then he returned.\n[Sad: 34]\nThe explanation about the trial of Sulaiman(as) is given in a sahih hadith as follows. One night Sulaiman(as) decided that he would go to all his wives who were about seventy to ninety and each one would bear him a son and all his sons would go on jihad in the path of Allah(swt). But he did not say ‘Insha Allah’ that is, ‘if Allah(swt) wills’. So, only one wife became pregnant and gave birth to a boy who only had half a body. When this body was placed on the throne, Sulaiman(as) realized his mistake and repented and sought the forgiveness of Allah(swt). It is said in the same hadith that if he had said, ‘Insha Allah’, then all his wives would have borne him sons who would’ve fought jihad in the path of Allah(swt)."],[310,"§Sun\nSun was one of the things considered to be god by the ancient people. But it is just one of the countless stars in the Universe. As it is the nearest star to the earth and the most beneficial to the creatures of earth, it has been described using various names and attributes. Some called it the incarnation of fire while some called it the lord of the Universe. Condemning all these blind beliefs, the Holy Quran describes the following story of Ibraheem(as):\n﴿فَلَمَّا جَنَّ عَلَيْهِ اللَّيْلُ رَأَىٰ كَوْكَبًا ۖ قَالَ هَـٰذَا رَبِّي ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَ قَالَ لَا أُحِبُّ الْآفِلِينَ ٧٦ فَلَمَّا رَأَى الْقَمَرَ بَازِغًا قَالَ هَـٰذَا رَبِّي ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَ قَالَ لَئِن لَّمْ يَهْدِنِي رَبِّي لَأَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الضَّالِّينَ ٧٧ فَلَمَّا رَأَى الشَّمْسَ بَازِغَةً قَالَ هَـٰذَا رَبِّي هَـٰذَا أَكْبَرُ ۖ فَلَمَّا أَفَلَتْ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ إِنِّي بَرِيءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُونَ ٧٨ إِنِّي وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِيَ لِلَّذِي فَطَرَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ حَنِيفًا ۖ وَمَا أَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ ٧٩﴾\nSo when the night covered him [with darkness], he saw a star. He said, \"This is my lord.\" But when it set, he said, \"I like not those that disappear.\" And when he saw the moon rising, he said, \"This is my lord.\" But when it set, he said, \"Unless my Lord guides me, I will surely be among the people gone astray.\" And when he saw the sun rising, he said, \"This is my lord; this is greater.\" But when it set, he said, \"O my people, indeed I am free from what you associate with Allah. Indeed, I have turned my face toward He who created the heavens and the earth, inclining toward truth, and I am not of those who associate others with Allah.\"\n[Al-An’am: 76-79]\n﴿وَمِنْ آيَاتِهِ اللَّيْلُ وَالنَّهَارُ وَالشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ ۚ لَا تَسْجُدُوا لِلشَّمْسِ وَلَا لِلْقَمَرِ وَاسْجُدُوا لِلَّـهِ الَّذِي خَلَقَهُنَّ إِن كُنتُمْ إِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُونَ ٣٧﴾\nAnd of His signs are the night and day and the sun and moon. Do not prostrate to the sun or to the moon, but prostrate to Allah, who created them, if it should be Him that you worship.\n[Ha-Meem As-Sajda: 37]"],[311,"§Surah\n‘Surah’ is the wall which encircles a city. In the same way, the wall surrounding a house is also called a ‘Surah’. The Holy Quran has 114 ‘Surahs’. These divisions are called ‘Surahs’ because they contain many issues within them.\nTo differentiate the different surahs, ‘Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim’ is written before every surah except the Surah-At-Tawba because it is the opinion of the scholars that it is a part of Surah-Al-Anfal.\nAt the beginning of every surah, Makkiy or Madani is written which means that it was revealed in Makkah or Madina."],[312,"§Suwaa\nThis was an idol of the tribe of Huzail. (For more information see ‘Wadd’.)"],[313,"§Swine\nEating the flesh of swine (See: Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-173; Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-3 and Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-115), rearing them and trading in them are all forbidden and unlawful in Islam because it is a filthy animal. Eating it was forbidden even in the Taurah (See: Leviticus, 11:7-8) and this same thing was preached by Isa(as) also. But when St. Paul took up Christianity, he made the flesh of swine lawful. When Isa(as) returns to earth, he will again make the flesh of swine unlawful and will kill the swine with his own hands as is narrated in the sahih hadith. (See: Sahih Bukhari:2222 and Sahih Muslim:155)\nIn the book Leviticus of the Taurah, the clean and unclean animals have been clearly described in part 11.\n“And the pig, though it has a divided hoof, does not chew the cud; it is unclean for you. You must not eat their meat or touch their carcasses; they are unclean for you.”\n(Taurah, Leviticus 11:7-8)"],[314,"§Taaboot\n‘Taaboot’ is a word of the Hebrew language which means ‘a wooden chest’. This is described at two places in the Holy Quran:\nFirst: The ‘Taaboot’ which the Bani-Israel brought with them during the exodus from Egypt and which they always kept with them. They would take it with them when they went to war and believed that it would give them victory. And they experienced peace and tranquility when they had the ‘Taaboot’ with them. In one war, the Palestinians were victorious and took away the ‘Taaboot’ from the Bani-Israel with them. Referring to this, the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَقَالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ إِنَّ آيَةَ مُلْكِهِ أَن يَأْتِيَكُمُ التَّابُوتُ فِيهِ سَكِينَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَبَقِيَّةٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ آلُ مُوسَىٰ وَآلُ هَارُونَ تَحْمِلُهُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ ۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَآيَةً لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ٢٤٨﴾\nAnd their prophet said to them, \"Indeed, a sign of his kingship is that the chest will come to you in which is assurance from your Lord and a remnant of what the family of Moses and the family of Aaron had left, carried by the angels. Indeed in that is a sign for you, if you are believers.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 248]\nThis was when the Bani-Israel pleaded with Samuel(as) to appoint a king for them under whose leadership they could defeat the Palestinians. When Samuel(as) made Talut(Saul) their king, they started denouncing him. Samuel(as) then told them that one of the signs of their true king would be that he would get back their ‘Taaboot’. A detailed description is given in the Bible about the ‘Taaboot’. It says that ‘Taaboot’ was made by Musa(as) as commanded by Allah(swt). It was made of acacia wood; two and a half cubits long, one and a half cubit wide and one and a half cubit deep. It had gold molding around it. It had two poles on each side so that it could be carried on the shoulders. And then it was covered with a cloth so that nobody could see it. (See: Exodus, 25:10)\nIn it were placed the staff of Haroon(as), the vessel which Musa(as) used to collect the ‘Manna’ which came down from the sky, the tablets on which were written the ten commandments and the first Torah scroll as written by Musa(as). The people who carried it were from the Levi tribe(the tribe to which Musa(as)’s father belonged). Whenever they went to war, the ‘Taaboot’ was carried before the army as a source of encouragement and it also gave them a sense of peace. Most of the times the Bani-Israel emerged victorious.\nIn one war, the Bani-Israel were defeated and the Palestinians took away the ‘Taaboot’ with them. They kept it in the temple of their god ‘Dajun’. Then, it came back to the Bani-Israel during the time of Talut or Saul. When Dawood(as) became the king, he made a tent and kept the ‘Taaboot’ in it. When Sulaiman(as) built the mosque, he placed the ‘Taaboot’ in a special chamber. (See: 2 Samuel, 6:1-10 and 1 Chronicles, 15:25)\nWhen the king of Babylon, ‘Bukht Nasar’ attacked the Jews around 600 B.C., he took away the ‘Taaboot’ with him which was destroyed with Yeroshalem because it could not be traced after that. Some people say that it is still present in Ethiopia. But there is no evidence of it. (See: Khamoos Muqaddas, p.209,210)\nSecond: The chest in which Musa(as)’s mother put him and set afloat in the river following the command of Allah(swt). This was to protect Musa(as) from the evil Pharaoh(Firaun) who was killing all new-born boys and letting the girls live. Musa(as)’s mother did as she was commanded and set the chest afloat in the water which was then retrieved by the wife of the Pharaoh(Firaun). She took the baby Musa(as) home and brought him up in the royal palace. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِذْ أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ أُمِّكَ مَا يُوحَىٰ ٣٨ أَنِ اقْذِفِيهِ فِي التَّابُوتِ فَاقْذِفِيهِ فِي الْيَمِّ فَلْيُلْقِهِ الْيَمُّ بِالسَّاحِلِ يَأْخُذْهُ عَدُوٌّ لِّي وَعَدُوٌّ لَّهُ ۚ وَأَلْقَيْتُ عَلَيْكَ مَحَبَّةً مِّنِّي وَلِتُصْنَعَ عَلَىٰ عَيْنِي ٣٩﴾\nWhen We inspired to your mother what We inspired, [Saying], 'Cast him into the chest and cast it into the river, and the river will throw it onto the bank; there will take him an enemy to Me and an enemy to him.' And I bestowed upon you love from Me that you would be brought up under My eye.\n[Ta-Ha: 38, 39]\nFor the remaining story about how Musa(as) reached his mother, see ‘Musa(as)’."],[315,"§Taaghoot\nThe word ‘Taaghoot’ has been used eight times in the Holy Quran:\nSurah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-256; Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verses-51,60,76; Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-60; Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-36 and Surah-39, Az-Zumar, Verse-17.\nIn all the verses the meaning is the same – worshipping something other than Allah(swt); be it humans, idols, satans – all are ‘Taaghoot’. The right to be worshipped is that of Allah(swt) alone and it cannot be given to other creatures or things which have been created by Allah(swt). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ ۖ قَد تَّبَيَّنَ الرُّشْدُ مِنَ الْغَيِّ ۚ فَمَن يَكْفُرْ بِالطَّاغُوتِ وَيُؤْمِن بِاللَّـهِ فَقَدِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقَىٰ لَا انفِصَامَ لَهَا ۗ وَاللَّـهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢٥٦﴾\nSo whoever disbelieves in Taghut and believes in Allah has grasped the most trustworthy handhold with no break in it.\n[Al-Baqara: 256]\n﴿اللَّـهُ وَلِيُّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا يُخْرِجُهُم مِّنَ الظُّلُمَاتِ إِلَى النُّورِ ۖ وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَوْلِيَاؤُهُمُ الطَّاغُوتُ يُخْرِجُونَهُم مِّنَ النُّورِ إِلَى الظُّلُمَاتِ ۗ أُولَـٰئِكَ أَصْحَابُ النَّارِ ۖ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ ٢٥٧﴾\nAllah is the ally of those who believe. He brings them out from darknesses into the light. And those who disbelieve - their allies are Taghut. They take them out of the light into darknesses. Those are the companions of the Fire; they will abide eternally therein.\n[Al-Baqara: 257]\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيبًا مِّنَ الْكِتَابِ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْجِبْتِ وَالطَّاغُوتِ وَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا هَـٰؤُلَاءِ أَهْدَىٰ مِنَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا سَبِيلًا ٥١﴾\nHave you not seen those who were given a portion of the Scripture, who believe in superstition and Taghut.\n[An-Nisa: 51]\nوَلَقَدْ بَعَثْنَا فِي كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ رَّسُولًا أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ وَاجْتَنِبُوا الطَّاغُوتَ\nAnd We certainly sent into every nation a messenger, [saying], \"Worship Allah and avoid Taghut.\"\n[An-Nahl: 36]\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ اجْتَنَبُوا الطَّاغُوتَ أَن يَعْبُدُوهَا وَأَنَابُوا إِلَى اللَّـهِ لَهُمُ الْبُشْرَىٰ ۚ فَبَشِّرْ عِبَادِ ١٧﴾\nBut those who have avoided Taghut, lest they worship it, and turned back to Allah - for them are good tidings. So give good tidings to My servants.\n[Az-Zumar: 17]"],[316,"§Talut\n‘Talut’ is the same person who is called ‘Saul’ in the Bible. It has been explained in the story of Dawood(as) how Saul became ‘Talut’.\nThe information we have about ‘Talut’ is as follows. When the Bani-Israel entered Palestine, they started facing many problems. The biggest problem was the war which started with the Palestinians and the people of the surrounding areas because the Bani-Israel had forcibly entered their area. They had committed many atrocities on the natives due to which they were furious with the Bani-Israel. At one time the Palestinians even defeated the Bani-Israel and snatched away their ‘Taaboot’ which they had brought with them from Egypt. As the Bani-Israel did not have a king, they were leading an undisciplined and chaotic life. So, they requested their prophet Samuel(as) to appoint a king for them who would lead them in wars against the Palestinians and other enemies. Samuel(as) warned the Bani-Israel not to appoint a king. But the Bani-Israel were stubborn that they wanted one as they had been driven out of their homes. Then the very thing which Samuel(as) had feared happened. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الْمَلَإِ مِن بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ مِن بَعْدِ مُوسَىٰ إِذْ قَالُوا لِنَبِيٍّ لَّهُمُ ابْعَثْ لَنَا مَلِكًا نُّقَاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ ۖ قَالَ هَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ إِن كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ أَلَّا تُقَاتِلُوا ۖ قَالُوا وَمَا لَنَا أَلَّا نُقَاتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ وَقَدْ أُخْرِجْنَا مِن دِيَارِنَا وَأَبْنَائِنَا ۖ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوْا إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّنْهُمْ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَلِيمٌ بِالظَّالِمِينَ ٢٤٦﴾\nHave you not considered the assembly of the Children of Israel after [the time of] Moses when they said to a prophet of theirs, \"Send to us a king, and we will fight in the way of Allah \"? He said, \"Would you perhaps refrain from fighting if fighting was prescribed for you?\" They said, \"And why should we not fight in the cause of Allah when we have been driven out from our homes and from our children?\" But when fighting was prescribed for them, they turned away, except for a few of them. And Allah is Knowing of the wrongdoers.\n[Al-Baqara: 246]\nUpon the insistence of the Bani-Israel, Samuel appointed a poor man Talut(Saul) from the tribe of Benjamin their king. The Bani-Israel complained, “You have made a poor man from the smallest tribe of Israel our king!” Samuel(as) said, “Allah(swt) had chosen Talut as your king because he is wise and strong.” The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَقَالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ قَدْ بَعَثَ لَكُمْ طَالُوتَ مَلِكًا ۚ قَالُوا أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ عَلَيْنَا وَنَحْنُ أَحَقُّ بِالْمُلْكِ مِنْهُ وَلَمْ يُؤْتَ سَعَةً مِّنَ الْمَالِ ۚ قَالَ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ اصْطَفَاهُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَزَادَهُ بَسْطَةً فِي الْعِلْمِ وَالْجِسْمِ ۖ وَاللَّـهُ يُؤْتِي مُلْكَهُ مَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَاللَّـهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢٤٧﴾\nAnd their prophet said to them, \"Indeed, Allah has sent to you Saul as a king.\" They said, \"How can he have kingship over us while we are more worthy of kingship than him and he has not been given any measure of wealth?\" He said, \"Indeed, Allah has chosen him over you and has increased him abundantly in knowledge and stature. And Allah gives His sovereignty to whom He wills. And Allah is all-Encompassing [in favor] and Knowing.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 247]\nTalut was the first king of the Bani-Israel. He constituted an army of young men and set out to fight the Palestinians as the Palestinians were getting ready for war. There was a man named Jalut(Goliath) in the Palestinian army who was very brave and strong. He was of a very huge build. He is described in the Bible as being six cubits tall and was fully armoured. (See: Bible, 1 Samuel, 17:4) Dawood(as) killed him with the help of a sling and a stone. (See: 1 Samuel: 17:49). Seeing this, the Palestinians started running away. The army of Talut chased and killed many of them. Talut made Dawood(as) his army-chief and gave his daughter to him in marriage. But when he realized that the Bani-Israel liked Dawood(as) more than him, he feared that Dawood(as) would take over his kingdom. So, he decided to kill Dawood(as). When Dawood(as) came to know of this he fled. In the war between the Bani-Israel and the Palestinians at a place called ‘Jalwu’a’, Talut and his three sons were killed. It is said that Talut committed suicide because he did not want to be captured and killed by the Palestinians. This happened around 1055 B.C. After that the people made Dawood(as) their king and he ruled over them till 1015 B.C. Thus, Dawood(as) is considered to be the first king among the prophets and the second king of the Bani-Israel."],[317,"§Tabook\n‘Tabook’ is a place located about 780 kilometers north of Madina. Its king Heraclius was a Christian and was against the spread of Islam. He wanted to propagate Christianity and considered Islam to be a great danger to his mission. So, he marched towards Madina with a one-lakh strong army. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know of this, he(saws) also readied his Muslim army and ordered them to march to Tabook. It was a very difficult period. It was during the months of June and July when hot winds were blowing across the desert and it was difficult to even come out of their houses. And moreover it was time for harvesting the dates and the Muslims were ordered to go to war. The Holy Quran itself says that it was indeed a difficult period:\n﴿لَّقَد تَّابَ اللَّـهُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالْأَنصَارِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِن بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيغُ قُلُوبُ فَرِيقٍ مِّنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّهُ بِهِمْ رَءُوفٌ رَّحِيمٌ ١١٧﴾\nAllah has already forgiven the Prophet and the Muhajireen and the Ansar who followed him in the hour of difficulty after the hearts of a party of them had almost inclined [to doubt], and then He forgave them. Indeed, He was to them Kind and Merciful.\n[At-Tawba: 117]\nWith complete faith in Allah(swt), the Muslims set forth. They neither had war equipment nor anything much to eat other than some dates. It is narrated in the sahih hadith that two men ate one date. But their hearts were filled with the love of Allah(swt) and the Holy Prophet(saws). They considered themselves lucky to be given a chance to sacrifice their lives for Allah(swt). They were not worried about their life in this world. The Prophet(saws) set out with an army of thirty thousand. There were no proper roads. They struggled through the mountains and reached Tabook. When Heraclius saw them, he lost his courage and agreed to pay ‘Jaziya’ tax and the other chieftains also agreed to do the same as a result of which there was no battle. The Holy Prophet(saws) stayed in Tabook for twenty days and then returned to Madina.\nIn this battle, the hypocrites displayed their true colours. On one hand they did not go forth to fight and on the other hand they tried to discourage the Muslims from going ahead. But they were not successful. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came back from Tabook, they came up to him to offer their excuses for not accompanying him. The Holy Prophet(saws) accepted them upon which the following verse was revealed:\n﴿عَفَا اللَّـهُ عَنكَ لِمَ أَذِنتَ لَهُمْ حَتَّىٰ يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكَ الَّذِينَ صَدَقُوا وَتَعْلَمَ الْكَاذِبِينَ ٤٣﴾\nMay Allah pardon you, [O Muhammad]; why did you give them permission [to remain behind]? [You should not have] until it was evident to you who were truthful and you knew [who were] the liars.\n[At-Tawba: 43]\nInitially Allah(swt) did not accept the repentance of three people: Kaab-bin-Maalik, Murara-bin-Rabi’a and Hilal-bin-Umaiya. But when they humbled themselves completely, heart and soul in front of Allah(swt), He(swt) forgave them. This is described in the Holy Quran as:\n﴿وَعَلَى الثَّلَاثَةِ الَّذِينَ خُلِّفُوا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ أَنفُسُهُمْ وَظَنُّوا أَن لَّا مَلْجَأَ مِنَ اللَّـهِ إِلَّا إِلَيْهِ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوبُوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ ١١٨﴾\nAnd [He also forgave] the three who were left behind [and regretted their error] to the point that the earth closed in on them in spite of its vastness and their souls confined them and they were certain that there is no refuge from Allah except in Him. Then He turned to them so they could repent. Indeed, Allah is the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.\n[At-Tawba: 118]\nFor a detailed description see ‘Three people who were left behind’."],[318,"§Ta-Ha\nSee: Alif-Laam-Meem."],[319,"§Talaq\n‘Talaq’ or ‘divorce’ is an unpleasant thing because the main aim of marriage is that the wife and husband should happily live together and take good care of their children. But sometimes the conditions become so unbearable that it becomes impossible for the wife and husband to live together and the only solution left would be ‘talaq’. This is an ancient practice. It is described in the Bible.\nIt says in ‘Luke’ Injeel:\nBut I tell you that anyone who divorces his wife, except for sexual immorality, makes her the victim of adultery, and anyone who marries a divorced woman commits adultery.\n(Matthew, 5:32)\nThat is, except in the case of adultery, a Christian cannot divorce his wife for any other reason. And even if he divorces her, no other man can marry her. With instructions like these, Christianity tried to put an end to the practice of divorce and formulated such tough rules which were impossible to implement.\nIslam is a moderate religion and follows the middle-path as the Holy Quran says:\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِّتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا ۗ\nAnd thus we have made you a just community that you will be witnesses over the people and the Messenger will be a witness over you.\n[Al-Baqara: 143]\nIslam, while describing ‘talaq’ as an extremely unpleasant thing, also says that it is compulsory under some circumstances and preferable under some conditions. When family life becomes unbearable due to some reason or the other and the husband and wife simply cannot live together, divorce is better than leading a painful life both in the case of the couple as well as in the case of their children.\nThe correct way of giving ‘talaq’:\nWhen ‘talaq’ becomes unavoidable, then the correct way of giving it is as follows: When the wife has completed her periods and has purified herself and the husband has not had intercourse with her, he should pronounce the first ‘talaq’. Then after the completion of the time during which she is pure when she again has her periods and then purifies herself, the husband should pronounce the second ‘talaq’. Then he should again wait for the next period and after she has purified herself, he should pronounce the third ‘talaq’. After this, the wife and husband will be permanently separated. This is called ‘talaq-e-bain’. After talaq-e-bain, if the wife marries someone else and after consummating the second marriage, the second husband divorces her, or if the second husband dies, then she can marry the first husband again and this is called ‘halala’. Without this second marriage she cannot remarry her first husband.\nThis period of three months has been kept so that if the husband and wife decide to get back together, then the husband can ‘ruzu’ or revoke the divorce. The method is as follows:\n1. He can say that he is doing ‘ruzu’ of talaq.\n2. He can have intercourse with his wife.\nIt should be borne in mind that during these three months, the wife cannot leave the husband’s house; nor can the husband make her leave his house. This condition has been put so that by staying together, sometimes the involved parties may realize their mistakes and decide to get back together.\nThe wrong way of giving ‘talaq’:\n1. It is wrong to pronounce ‘talaq’ when the wife is having her periods. When Ibn-Umar(ra) pronounced ‘talaq’ to his wife when she was having her periods, the Holy Prophet(saws) asked him to ‘ruzu’ the ‘talaq’. Then after she was pure, he could pronounce it if he wished to do so. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 5252 and Sahih Muslim, 1471)\nBut if the husband pronounces the ‘talaq’ when the wife is menstruating, is it valid or not? Scholars differ in their views in this matter. But the correct version is that it will be counted as one ‘talaq’ as Ibn-Umar(ra) himself has narrated that it will be counted. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 5333 and Sahih Muslim, 1471)\n2. Pronouncing ‘talaq’ in a month after she is pure but when intercourse has taken place but she has not conceived. A man doing this will be a sinner but the ‘talaq’ is counted.\n3. Pronouncing more than one ‘talaq’ at the same time is a sin. When someone pronounces ‘talaq’ thrice at one time, will they be counted as three or not? Even in this matter there is a difference of opinion among the scholars. In the opinion of the author, it will be counted as one. For detailed information refer to the author’s Arabic book ‘Al-Minnatul-Kubra’."],[320,"§Taqwa\n‘Taqwa’ means ‘to fear’. This word has been used in the Holy Quran to explain the concept of fearing Allah(swt). Fearing Allah(swt) means to follow the path shown by Him. It means following His commands and abstaining and keeping away from the forbidden things. Among the commands to be followed are offering salah, giving zakat, fasting during the month of Ramadan, performing Hajj if one can afford to do so, helping each other, having good relations with one’s relatives, giving alms to the poor etc. The forbidden things are adultery, stealing, killing, giving false testimony, tormenting somebody etc. The best person is the one who fears Allah(swt) the most. The Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّ أَكْرَمَكُمْ عِندَ اللَّهِ أَتْقَاكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ خَبِيرٌ\nIndeed, the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous of you. Indeed, Allah is Knowing and Acquainted.\n[Al-Hujurat: 13]\nOnly the ‘Muttaqi’(people who fear Allah(swt)) people can benefit from the book of Allah(swt), the Holy Quran.\n﴿ذَٰلِكَ الْكِتَابُ لَا رَيْبَ ۛ فِيهِ ۛ هُدًى لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ ٢﴾\nThis is the Book about which there is no doubt, a guidance for those conscious of Allah.\n[Al-Baqara: 2]\nFor the people who fear Him, Allah(swt) has promised to open up ways:\nوَمَن يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُ مَخْرَجًا\nAnd whoever fears Allah - He will make for him a way out.\n[At-Talaq: 2]\nوَمَن يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُ مِنْ أَمْرِهِ يُسْرًا\nAnd whoever fears Allah - He will make for him of his matter ease.\n[At-Talaq: 4]\nAnd only the ones who fear Allah(swt) will be successful:\n﴿وَمَن يُطِعِ اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَيَخْشَ اللَّـهَ وَيَتَّقْهِ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْفَائِزُونَ ٥٢﴾\nAnd whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger and fears Allah and is conscious of Him - it is those who are the attainers.\n[An-Nur: 52]\nSo, the successful people are the ones who follow the path of Allah(swt) and listen to what the Holy Prophet(saws) instructs them:\nوَمَا آتَاكُمُ الرَّسُولُ فَخُذُوهُ وَمَا نَهَاكُمْ عَنْهُ فَانتَهُوا ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقَابِ\nAnd whatever the Messenger has given you - take; and what he has forbidden you - refrain from. And fear Allah; indeed, Allah is severe in penalty.\n[Al-Hashr: 7]"],[321,"§Tasbeeh\n‘Tasbeeh’ is a word specific to Islamic terminology and it is difficult to translate it into any other language because no other religion has a word which expresses the same meaning as expressed by ‘tasbeeh’ in the Holy Quran. This is because in every religion, ‘shirk’ or ‘polytheism’ is found in some form or the other and ‘tasbeeh’ expresses the Oneness of Allah(swt). ‘Tasbeeh’ means to glorify Allah(swt) and express His Oneness and Greatness as against all forms of ‘shirk’. Because He(swt) is the sole Creator of this vast Universe, everything in this Creation is glorifying(‘tasbeeh’) Allah(swt) in some form or the other.\nAngels doing the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt):\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنِّي جَاعِلٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً ۖ قَالُوا أَتَجْعَلُ فِيهَا مَن يُفْسِدُ فِيهَا وَيَسْفِكُ الدِّمَاءَ وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ ۖ قَالَ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ٣٠﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when your Lord said to the angels, \"Indeed, I will make upon the earth a successive authority.\" They said, \"Will You place upon it one who causes corruption therein and sheds blood, while we declare Your praise and sanctify You?\" Allah said, \"Indeed, I know that which you do not know.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 30]\nوَتَرَى الْمَلَائِكَةَ حَافِّينَ مِنْ حَوْلِ الْعَرْشِ يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ\nAnd you will see the angels surrounding the Throne, exalting [Allah] with praise of their Lord.\n[Az-Zumar: 75]\n﴿وَإِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الصَّافُّونَ ١٦٥ وَإِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْمُسَبِّحُونَ ١٦٦﴾\nAnd indeed, we are those who line up [for prayer]. And indeed, we are those who exalt Allah.\"\n[As-Saffat: 165, 166]\nClouds doing the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt):\nوَيُسَبِّحُ الرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهِ وَالْمَلَائِكَةُ مِنْ خِيفَتِهِ\nAnd the thunder exalts [Allah] with praise of Him - and the angels [as well] from fear of Him.\n[Ar-Ra’d: 13]\nMountains doing the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt):\n﴿إِنَّا سَخَّرْنَا الْجِبَالَ مَعَهُ يُسَبِّحْنَ بِالْعَشِيِّ وَالْإِشْرَاقِ ١٨﴾\nIndeed, We subjected the mountains [to praise] with him, exalting [Allah] in the [late] afternoon and [after] sunrise.\n[Sad: 18]\nBirds doing the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt):\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّ اللَّـهَ يُسَبِّحُ لَهُ مَن فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَالطَّيْرُ صَافَّاتٍ ۖ كُلٌّ قَدْ عَلِمَ صَلَاتَهُ وَتَسْبِيحَهُ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَلِيمٌ بِمَا يَفْعَلُونَ ٤١﴾\nDo you not see that Allah is exalted by whomever is within the heavens and the earth and [by] the birds with wings spread [in flight]? Each [of them] has known his [means of] prayer and exalting [Him], and Allah is Knowing of what they do.\n[An-Nur: 41]\nThat is, the entire Creation is doing the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt). But we cannot perceive it:\n﴿تُسَبِّحُ لَهُ السَّمَاوَاتُ السَّبْعُ وَالْأَرْضُ وَمَن فِيهِنَّ ۚ وَإِن مِّن شَيْءٍ إِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهِ وَلَـٰكِن لَّا تَفْقَهُونَ تَسْبِيحَهُمْ ۗ إِنَّهُ كَانَ حَلِيمًا غَفُورًا ٤٤﴾\nThe seven heavens and the earth and whatever is in them exalt Him. And there is not a thing except that it exalts [Allah] by His praise, but you do not understand their [way of] exalting. Indeed, He is ever Forbearing and Forgiving.\n[Bani-Israel: 44]\n‘Tasbeeh’ has been explained as our main aim in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith:\n﴿فِي بُيُوتٍ أَذِنَ اللَّـهُ أَن تُرْفَعَ وَيُذْكَرَ فِيهَا اسْمُهُ يُسَبِّحُ لَهُ فِيهَا بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْآصَالِ ٣٦ رِجَالٌ لَّا تُلْهِيهِمْ تِجَارَةٌ وَلَا بَيْعٌ عَن ذِكْرِ اللَّـهِ وَإِقَامِ الصَّلَاةِ وَإِيتَاءِ الزَّكَاةِ ۙ يَخَافُونَ يَوْمًا تَتَقَلَّبُ فِيهِ الْقُلُوبُ وَالْأَبْصَارُ ٣٧﴾\n[Such niches are] in mosques which Allah has ordered to be raised and that His name be mentioned therein; exalting Him within them in the morning and the evenings. [Are] men whom neither commerce nor sale distracts from the remembrance of Allah and performance of prayer and giving of zakah. They fear a Day in which the hearts and eyes will [fearfully] turn about.\n[An-Nur: 36, 37]\nMosques are the places where Allah(swt) is worshipped and exalted and glorified(tasbeeh). This is the description of those people whose hearts always beat with the remembrance of Allah(swt) and do the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt) which is:\n‘Subhan Allah, Subhan Allah’ that is, all Greatness and Purity is for Allah(swt) and He(swt) has no partners in it. But the people who do not realize it make some creature or the other His partner. For example someone makes somebody His son(Inna Aoozu Billah). It says in the Holy Quran:\nسُبْحَانَهُ أَن يَكُونَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ ۘ لَّهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ ۗ وَكَفَىٰ بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلًا\nExalted is He above having a son. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And sufficient is Allah as Disposer of affairs.\n[An-Nisa: 171]\n﴿وَقَالُوا اتَّخَذَ الرَّحْمَـٰنُ وَلَدًا ۗ سُبْحَانَهُ ۚ بَلْ عِبَادٌ مُّكْرَمُونَ ٢٦﴾\nAnd they say, \"The Most Merciful has taken a son.\" Exalted is He! Rather, they are [but] honored servants.\n[An-Anbiya: 26]\nThat is, these foolish people mistake the honoured angels who exalt and glorify Allah(swt) to be His sons. Moreover these people who have strayed attribute daughters to Allah(swt). (Inna Aoozu Billah). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَيَجْعَلُونَ لِلَّـهِ الْبَنَاتِ سُبْحَانَهُ ۙ وَلَهُم مَّا يَشْتَهُونَ ٥٧﴾\nAnd they attribute to Allah daughters - exalted is He - and for them is what they desire.\n[An-Nahl: 57]\nThat is, the polytheist Arabs did not want daughters for themselves but attributed daughters to Allah(swt) (Inna Aoozu Billah) whom they worshipped. Allah(swt) is pure and above what they attribute to Him. We should always remember Allah(swt) and do his tasbeeh as has been said again and again in the Holy Quran (See: Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-41; Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-130; Surah-40, Al-Momin, Verse-55 etc.) That is why every Muslim in his namaz says ‘Subhana Rabbiyal Azeem’ in the ‘ruku’ and ‘Subhana Rabbiyal Aala’ while prostrating – that is, I do the ‘tasbeeh’ of the Greatest Allah(swt).\nIn this way, by means of ‘tasbeeh’, Allah(swt) has closed all the ways leading to shirk as the ‘tasbeeh’ can be done only of Allah(swt) and it is in fact a form of worship. On various occasions Allah(swt) has commanded the Holy Prophet(saws) to do His ‘tasbeeh’ as it says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّـهِ وَالْفَتْحُ ١ وَرَأَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ اللَّـهِ أَفْوَاجًا ٢ فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ تَوَّابًا ٣﴾\nWhen the victory(help) of Allah has come and the conquest, And you see the people entering into the religion of Allah in multitudes, Then exalt [Him] with praise of your Lord and ask forgiveness of Him. Indeed, He is ever Accepting of repentance.\n[An-Nasr: 1-3]\nThis verse was revealed after the triumph over Makkah. This is Makkah from where the hard-hearted people had expelled the Holy Prophet(saws) just because he(saws) called them to the path of Allah(swt). And with the help of Allah(swt) he (saws) came back to his favourite city and people were accepting Islam in large groups. On this occasion he(saws) has been asked to exalt and glorify Allah(swt) and do His tasbeeh as Allah(swt) granted him victory over the disbelievers. That is, he(saws) should do the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt) alone. The importance of ‘tasbeeh’ has been mentioned in the sahih hadith also:\n“The sins of the one who says ‘Subhan Allahi wa biHamdihi’ a hundred times everyday, will be wiped out even if they are as many as the foam of the ocean.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 6405 and Sahih Muslim, 2691)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“There are two words which are very easy to say but are heavy in the balance and very dear with ‘Rehman’ and they are ‘SubhanAllah hil Azeem’ and ‘SubhanAllahi wa Bihamdihi’. (Sahih Bukhari, 6406 and Sahih Muslim, 2694)\nThat is, every Muslim should do the ‘tasbeeh’ every morning and evening and after every namaz(that is, say SubhanAllah, SubhanAllah) so that Allah(swt) is pleased and he gets the rewards both in this life and in the Hereafter. If Yunus(as) had not done the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt), he would have remained in the belly of the fish till Doomsday. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيمٌ ١٤٢ فَلَوْلَا أَنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِينَ ١٤٣ لَلَبِثَ فِي بَطْنِهِ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ ١٤٤﴾\nThen the fish swallowed him, while he was blameworthy. And had he not been of those who exalt Allah, He would have remained inside its belly until the Day they are resurrected.\n[As-Saffat: 142-144]\nAnd his ‘tasbeeh’ and supplication is also described in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَذَا النُّونِ إِذ ذَّهَبَ مُغَاضِبًا فَظَنَّ أَن لَّن نَّقْدِرَ عَلَيْهِ فَنَادَىٰ فِي الظُّلُمَاتِ أَن لَّا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا أَنتَ سُبْحَانَكَ إِنِّي كُنتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ ٨٧ فَاسْتَجَبْنَا لَهُ وَنَجَّيْنَاهُ مِنَ الْغَمِّ ۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نُنجِي الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ٨٨﴾\nAnd [mention] the man of the fish, when he went off in anger and thought that We would not decree [anything] upon him. And he called out within the darknesses, \"There is no deity except You; exalted are You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers.\" So We responded to him and saved him from the distress. And thus do We save the believers.\n[Al-Anbiya: 87, 88]\nWe understand from this that the previous prophets also did the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt). For example Musa(as) (See: Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-143), Isa(as) (See: Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-116)\nAnd the best thing is that the people who enter the paradise will say ‘SubhanAllah’. (See: Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-10) and it is narrated in the sahih hadith also that their hearts will be one and they shall glorify and exalt Allah(swt) (tasbeeh) morning and evening. (See: Sahih Muslim, 3834) and it is narrated in another sahih hadith that they shall do ‘tasbeeh’ just as we breathe continuously. (See: Sahih Muslim, 3838)\nThat is why no Muslim should neglect doing the ‘tasbeeh’ of Allah(swt)."]])